/-!
# Ch. IV §1 (pp. 275–286): localization of resolution data and resolution problems

Chapter IV opens (pp. 274–275):

> In this chapter, we shall often find it convenient to express a resolution datum of type
> ℜ^{N,n}_I on a non-singular irreducible algebraic scheme X in the following form:
>
>     ℜ^{N,n}_I = (⋃_{i=1}^α E_i; V₁, V₂, …, V_β; W).
>
> We agree once for all that *whenever this expression is taken, all the E_i denote
> non-singular irreducible subschemes of X of codimension one*. …
>
> In the treatment of a resolution datum of type ℜ^N_II on a non-singular irreducible
> algebraic scheme X, say ℜ^N_II = (E₁, E₂, …, E_α | J, b | a₁, a₂, …, a_α), all that are
> essential among its characteristics are the following ones: the set C(ℜ^N_II) of those
> irreducible subschemes E_i of X which are not empty, the integers a(E) = ∑_{E_i = E} a_i
> for E ∈ C(ℜ^N_II), J and b. …

and §1 itself opens (pp. 275–276):

> Let f: X' → X be a morphism of algebraic schemes, which is of finite type; … Take a point x
> of X and the local ring S of X at x. … We have a canonical immersion i: Spec(S) → X, …
> This permits us to identify Spec(S) with the restriction of X to the
> set of those points of X whose closures contain x, i.e., x is a *specialization* of those
> points in X. The product of the schemes X' and Spec(S) over X (with reference to f and i)
> will be denoted by X'_S (or, by (X')_S). … We have a canonical immersion
> j: X'_S → X', … In an obvious manner, a subscheme of X' induces a subscheme of X'_S
> and every subscheme of X'_S is obtained in this way. …

Contents: the localization `X'_S` and of subschemes and subsets (pp. 275–276, with the
assertions of those two pages collected in `lem:IV.1-localize-basic`), Definition 1
(`def:IV.1`, `def:IV.1-II`), Remarks 1 and 2, Lemmas 1 and 2 and the four localization
theorems, Propositions 1–4.  The constructions shared by the proofs of Propositions 1–4 (the
lifting "(1)–(3)" of p. 279 of a succession of `X'_S` to a succession of `X'`) are in
`Hironaka/Compat/LocalizeSuccession.lean` (type I) and `Hironaka/Compat/LocalizeSuccessionII.lean`
(type II).

Conventions and formalization notes (each is repeated at the node it concerns).
* `Spec(S) → X` is Mathlib's `X.fromSpecStalk x` (its range is `{y | y ⤳ x}`,
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.range_fromSpecStalk`, which is exactly Hironaka's "the set of
  those points of X whose closures contain x"), and `X'_S` is the pullback of `f` along it,
  i.e. the product of `X'` and `Spec S` over `X`, as in the paper.
* The subscheme of `X'_S` induced by `Y' ⊆ X'` is the total transform of `Y'` along
  `j : X'_S → X'` (the sheaf of ideals generated by that of `Y'`, footnote 35, p. 168);
  since `j` is flat this is the restriction of the sheaf of ideals of `Y'`, which is how the
  paper describes `J'_S` in Definition 1 (II).
* `f` of finite type is `[LocallyOfFiniteType f] [QuasiCompact f]`, the two conditions used
  in `IsAlgebraicScheme` (Ch. 0).
* The statements of the paper are transcribed as written; representation choices are flagged
  "Formalization note (encoding)", and every departure from the paper's statements or proofs
  is flagged "Deviation from the paper (…)", "Correction of the paper (…)", "Gap in the paper
  filled" or "Paper misprint".
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits AlgebraicGeometry TopologicalSpace

namespace Hironaka

universe u

/-! ### The chapter's expression `ℜ^{N,n}_I = (⋃_{i=1}^α E_i; V₁, …, V_β; W)` (pp. 274–275) -/

/-- The agreement of pp. 274–275: a datum of type `ℜ^{N,n}_I` is written in the form
`(⋃_{i=1}^α E_i; V₁, …, V_β; W)`, and "whenever this expression is taken, all the `E_i`
denote non-singular irreducible subschemes of `X` of codimension one", repetitions and the
empty subscheme being allowed.  The union is the subscheme defined by the intersection of the
ideal sheaves (p. 165), as in `DatumII.Raw.eUnion`.

Formalization note (encoding): this predicate records the notation, not a restriction of the
paper's generality: the irreducible components of a reduced subscheme which is everywhere of
codimension one and has only normal crossings are non-singular of codimension one, and `E` is
their union.  It is carried as a hypothesis by the nodes in which the paper writes a datum in
this form (`lem:IV.1-1`, `prop:IV.1-1`, `prop:IV.1-2`), but none of their proofs uses it. -/
def DatumI.Raw.IsUnionOfDivisors {X : Scheme.{u}} (ℜ : DatumI.Raw X) : Prop :=
  ∃ (α : ℕ) (E : Fin α → Subscheme X),
    (∀ i, (E i).IsNonsingularIrreducibleCodimOne) ∧ ℜ.E = ⨅ i, E i

/-! ### The localization `X'_S` (pp. 275–276) -/

/-- The localization `X'_S` of `X'` at the point `x` of `X`: "the product of the schemes `X'`
and `Spec(S)` over `X` (with reference to `f` and `i`) will be denoted by `X'_S`", where `S`
is the local ring of `X` at `x` and `i : Spec(S) → X` is the canonical immersion (p. 275).
Here `i` is `X.fromSpecStalk x`, whose range is the set of points of `X` whose closures
contain `x` (`Scheme.range_fromSpecStalk`), and the product over `X` is the pullback. -/
@[blueprint "def:IV.1-localize-scheme"
  (statement := /-- Let $f\colon X'\to X$ be a morphism of algebraic schemes of finite type,
    $x$ a point of $X$ and $S$ the local ring of $X$ at $x$. There is a canonical immersion
    $i\colon\operatorname{Spec}(S)\to X$ mapping the unique closed point of
    $\operatorname{Spec}(S)$ to $x$, which identifies $\operatorname{Spec}(S)$ with the
    restriction of $X$ to the set of those points of $X$ whose closures contain $x$. The
    product of the schemes $X'$ and $\operatorname{Spec}(S)$ over $X$ (with reference to $f$
    and $i$) is denoted by $X'_S$ (or $(X')_S$); it is the product in the category of schemes
    over the fixed scheme $X$. There is a canonical immersion $j\colon X'_S\to X'$, which
    identifies $X'_S$ with the restriction of $X'$ to the set of those points of $X'$ which
    belong to $f^{-1}(\operatorname{Spec}(S))$. (pp.\ 275–276.)

    Formalization note (encoding): $i$ is Mathlib's $X.\mathrm{fromSpecStalk}\,x$, whose range is
    the set of generizations of $x$, and $X'_S$ is the pullback of $f$ along it; the canonical
    immersion $j$ is the first projection, an embedding with bijective stalk maps. -/)
  (latexEnv := "definition")]
noncomputable def localizeScheme {X X' : Scheme.{u}} (f : X' ⟶ X) (x : X) : Scheme.{u} :=
  pullback f (X.fromSpecStalk x)

/-- The canonical immersion `j : X'_S → X'` of p. 275, i.e. the first projection of the
product of `X'` and `Spec(S)` over `X`. -/
noncomputable def localizeMap {X X' : Scheme.{u}} (f : X' ⟶ X) (x : X) :
    localizeScheme f x ⟶ X' :=
  pullback.fst f (X.fromSpecStalk x)

/-- "In an obvious manner, a subscheme of `X'` induces a subscheme of `X'_S` and every
subscheme of `X'_S` is obtained in this way" (p. 275): the subscheme `Y'_S` of `X'_S` induced
by a subscheme `Y'` of `X'`.

Formalization note (encoding): the induced subscheme is realized as the total transform of
`Y'` along `j : X'_S → X'` (the subscheme of `X'_S` defined by the sheaf of ideals generated by
that of `Y'`, footnote 35, p. 168).  Because `j` is flat this is the restriction to `X'_S` of
the sheaf of ideals of `Y'`, which is the description used in Definition 1 (II) for `J'_S`.

"If `Y'` is a subscheme of `X'`, then the subscheme of `X'_S` induced by `Y'` is canonically
isomorphic to `Y'_S` (which denotes the product `Y'` and `Spec(S)` over `X`)": this is
`Subscheme.localizeIso` below (the node `lem:IV.1-localize-subscheme-product`). -/
@[blueprint "def:IV.1-localize-subscheme"
  (statement := /-- In an obvious manner, a subscheme of $X'$ induces a subscheme of $X'_S$,
    and every subscheme of $X'_S$ is obtained in this way. If $Y'$ is a subscheme of $X'$,
    then the subscheme of $X'_S$ induced by $Y'$ is canonically isomorphic to $Y'_S$ (which
    denotes the product of $Y'$ and $\operatorname{Spec}(S)$ over $X$), so that we can view
    $Y'_S$ as the subscheme of $X'_S$ induced by $Y'$. (p.\ 275.)

    Formalization note (encoding): the induced subscheme is the total transform of $Y'$ along
    the canonical immersion $j\colon X'_S\to X'$, i.e.\ (as $j$ is flat) the restriction of the
    sheaf of ideals of $Y'$ to $X'_S$. The canonical isomorphism with the product
    $Y'\times_X\operatorname{Spec}(S)$ is \cref{lem:IV.1-localize-subscheme-product}; that every
    subscheme of $X'_S$ is induced is part of \cref{lem:IV.1-localize-basic}. -/)
  (latexEnv := "definition")]
noncomputable def Subscheme.localize {X X' : Scheme.{u}} (f : X' ⟶ X) (x : X)
    (Y' : Subscheme X') : Subscheme (localizeScheme f x) :=
  Subscheme.totalTransform (localizeMap f x) Y'

/-- The subscheme `Y'_S` of `X'_S` induced by `Y'` is the base change of the closed immersion
`Y' → X'` along `j`, i.e. the fibre product of `X'_S` and `Y'` over `X'` (the total transform is
the kernel of the base change, `Subscheme.totalTransform`; `Scheme.IdealSheafData.comapIso`). -/
noncomputable def Subscheme.localizeComapIso {X X' : Scheme.{u}} (f : X' ⟶ X) (x : X)
    (Y' : Subscheme X') :
    (Y'.localize f x).toScheme ≅ pullback (pullback.fst f (X.fromSpecStalk x)) Y'.ι :=
  Scheme.IdealSheafData.comapIso Y' (localizeMap f x)

@[reassoc (attr := simp)]
theorem Subscheme.localizeComapIso_hom_fst {X X' : Scheme.{u}} (f : X' ⟶ X) (x : X)
    (Y' : Subscheme X') :
    (Subscheme.localizeComapIso f x Y').hom ≫ pullback.fst _ _ = (Y'.localize f x).ι :=
  Scheme.IdealSheafData.comapIso_hom_fst Y' (localizeMap f x)

/-- "If `Y'` is a subscheme of `X'`, then the subscheme of `X'_S` induced by `Y'` is canonically
isomorphic to `Y'_S` (which denotes the product `Y'` and `Spec(S)` over `X`)" (p. 275): the
canonical isomorphism `(Y'_S) ≅ Y' ×_X Spec(S)`, the product being the fibre product of
`Y' → X' → X` and `i : Spec(S) → X` (`X.fromSpecStalk x`).  It is the composite of the base change
description of the induced subscheme (`Subscheme.localizeComapIso`) with the pasting isomorphism
`Y' ×_{X'} (X' ×_X Spec(S)) ≅ Y' ×_X Spec(S)`; the two projections of the product are the
restriction of `j` to `Y'_S` followed by the inclusion of `Y'` and the second projection of
`X'_S` (`localizeIso_hom_fst_ι`, `localizeIso_hom_snd`).  Gap filled. -/
@[blueprint "lem:IV.1-localize-subscheme-product"
  (statement := /-- Let $f\colon X'\to X$ be a morphism of schemes, $x$ a point of $X$,
    $S$ the local ring of $X$ at $x$, $i\colon\operatorname{Spec}(S)\to X$ the canonical
    immersion and $j\colon X'_S\to X'$ the canonical immersion. If $Y'$ is a subscheme of $X'$,
    then the subscheme $Y'_S$ of $X'_S$ induced by $Y'$ is canonically isomorphic to the product
    $Y'\times_X\operatorname{Spec}(S)$ of $Y'$ and $\operatorname{Spec}(S)$ over $X$ (with
    reference to $Y'\to X'\to X$ and $i$), the isomorphism being compatible with the
    projections: the first projection corresponds to the restriction of $j$, followed by the
    inclusion of $Y'$, and the second to that of $X'_S\to\operatorname{Spec}(S)$. (p.~275.) -/)
  (proof := /-- The subscheme of $X'_S$ induced by $Y'$ is defined by the sheaf of ideals
    generated by that of $Y'$, that is, it is the base change of the closed immersion
    $Y'\to X'$ along $j$: $Y'_S=Y'\times_{X'}X'_S$. Since $X'_S=X'\times_X\operatorname{Spec}(S)$,
    the pasting of fibre products gives
    $Y'\times_{X'}(X'\times_X\operatorname{Spec}(S))\cong Y'\times_X\operatorname{Spec}(S)$,
    compatibly with the projections. \textbf{Gap filled.} The paper asserts this as obvious. -/)
  (latexEnv := "definition")]
noncomputable def Subscheme.localizeIso {X X' : Scheme.{u}} (f : X' ⟶ X) (x : X)
    (Y' : Subscheme X') :
    (Y'.localize f x).toScheme ≅ pullback (Y'.ι ≫ f) (X.fromSpecStalk x) :=
  Subscheme.localizeComapIso f x Y' ≪≫ pullbackSymmetry _ _ ≪≫
    pullbackRightPullbackFstIso f (X.fromSpecStalk x) Y'.ι

theorem Subscheme.localizeIso_hom_fst_ι {X X' : Scheme.{u}} (f : X' ⟶ X) (x : X)
    (Y' : Subscheme X') :
    (Subscheme.localizeIso f x Y').hom ≫ pullback.fst _ _ ≫ Y'.ι =
      (Y'.localize f x).ι ≫ localizeMap f x := by
  unfold Subscheme.localizeIso
  simp only [Iso.trans_hom, Category.assoc, pullbackRightPullbackFstIso_hom_fst_assoc,
    pullbackSymmetry_hom_comp_fst_assoc]
  rw [← pullback.condition, ← Category.assoc, Subscheme.localizeComapIso_hom_fst]
  rfl

theorem Subscheme.localizeIso_hom_snd {X X' : Scheme.{u}} (f : X' ⟶ X) (x : X)
    (Y' : Subscheme X') :
    (Subscheme.localizeIso f x Y').hom ≫ pullback.snd _ _ =
      (Y'.localize f x).ι ≫ pullback.snd f (X.fromSpecStalk x) := by
  unfold Subscheme.localizeIso
  simp only [Iso.trans_hom, Category.assoc, pullbackRightPullbackFstIso_hom_snd,
    pullbackSymmetry_hom_comp_snd_assoc]
  rw [← Category.assoc, Subscheme.localizeComapIso_hom_fst]
  rfl

/-- The first projection `Y'_S → Y'` of the product `Y'_S = Y' ×_X Spec(S)` (p. 275). -/
noncomputable def Subscheme.localizeProj {X X' : Scheme.{u}} (f : X' ⟶ X) (x : X)
    (Y' : Subscheme X') : (Y'.localize f x).toScheme ⟶ Y'.toScheme :=
  (Subscheme.localizeIso f x Y').hom ≫ pullback.fst (Y'.ι ≫ f) (X.fromSpecStalk x)

/-- "Also in an obvious manner, an open (resp. closed) subset `H` of `X'` induces an open
(resp. closed) subset of `X'_S`, which we denote by `H_S`" (p. 276): the preimage of `H`
under the canonical immersion `j`. -/
def localizeSet {X X' : Scheme.{u}} (f : X' ⟶ X) (x : X) (H : Set X') :
    Set (localizeScheme f x) :=
  (localizeMap f x).base ⁻¹' H

section LocalizeInfra

variable {X X' : Scheme.{u}} (f : X' ⟶ X) (x : X)

private theorem flat_localizeMap : Flat (localizeMap f x) := by
  have := flat_fromSpecStalk X x
  unfold localizeMap localizeScheme
  infer_instance

private theorem isPreimmersion_localizeMap : IsPreimmersion (localizeMap f x) := by
  unfold localizeMap localizeScheme
  infer_instance

private theorem range_localizeMap :
    Set.range (localizeMap f x).base = f.base ⁻¹' {y : X | y ⤳ x} := by
  unfold localizeMap localizeScheme
  rw [Scheme.Pullback.range_fst, Scheme.range_fromSpecStalk]

private theorem mem_range_localizeMap_of_specializes {z w : X'} (hwz : w ⤳ z)
    (hz : z ∈ Set.range (localizeMap f x).base) : w ∈ Set.range (localizeMap f x).base := by
  rw [range_localizeMap] at hz ⊢
  exact (hwz.map f.base.hom.continuous).trans hz

/-- The stalk maps of `j : X'_S → X'` are bijective. -/
private theorem stalkMap_localizeMap_bijective (y : localizeScheme f x) :
    Function.Bijective ((localizeMap f x).stalkMap y).hom := by
  have := flat_localizeMap f x
  have := isPreimmersion_localizeMap f x
  refine ⟨?_, (localizeMap f x).stalkMap_surjective y⟩
  let _ : Algebra (X'.presheaf.stalk ((localizeMap f x) y))
      ((localizeScheme f x).presheaf.stalk y) :=
    ((localizeMap f x).stalkMap y).hom.toAlgebra
  have : Module.Flat (X'.presheaf.stalk ((localizeMap f x) y))
      ((localizeScheme f x).presheaf.stalk y) := Flat.stalkMap (localizeMap f x) y
  have : IsLocalHom (algebraMap (X'.presheaf.stalk ((localizeMap f x) y))
      ((localizeScheme f x).presheaf.stalk y)) := by
    show IsLocalHom ((localizeMap f x).stalkMap y).hom
    infer_instance
  have hff := Module.FaithfullyFlat.of_flat_of_isLocalHom
    (A := X'.presheaf.stalk ((localizeMap f x) y)) (B := (localizeScheme f x).presheaf.stalk y)
  exact (RingHom.faithfullyFlat_algebraMap_iff.mpr hff).injective

/-- The stalk isomorphism `O_{X', j y} ≅ O_{X'_S, y}`. -/
private noncomputable def localizeStalkEquiv (y : localizeScheme f x) :
    X'.presheaf.stalk ((localizeMap f x) y) ≃+* (localizeScheme f x).presheaf.stalk y :=
  RingEquiv.ofBijective _ (stalkMap_localizeMap_bijective f x y)

private theorem stalkIdeal_localize (Y' : Subscheme X') (y : localizeScheme f x) :
    (Y'.localize f x).stalkIdeal y =
      (Y'.stalkIdeal ((localizeMap f x) y)).map (localizeStalkEquiv f x y) :=
  stalkIdeal_totalTransform _ _ _

private theorem pts_localize (Y' : Subscheme X') :
    (Y'.localize f x).pts = (localizeMap f x).base ⁻¹' Y'.pts := by
  change ((Y'.comap (localizeMap f x)).support : Set (localizeScheme f x)) = _
  rw [Scheme.IdealSheafData.support_comap]
  rfl

end LocalizeInfra

section LocalizeCanonical

variable {X X' : Scheme.{u}} (f : X' ⟶ X) (x : X)

/-- "For every point `y` of `Y'_S`, which is also viewed as a point of `Y'`, the local ring of
`Y'_S` at `y` is equal to (or, more precisely, canonically isomorphic to) the local ring of `Y'`
at `y`" (p. 275–276): the canonical isomorphism is the stalk map at `y` of the projection
`Y'_S = Y' ×_X Spec(S) → Y'` (`Subscheme.localizeProj`), which is bijective.  Since the projection
of `Y'_S` is the base change of the flat preimmersion `Spec(S) → X` along `Y' → X`, this is the
bijectivity of the stalk maps of `j` (`stalkMap_localizeMap_bijective`) for the morphism
`Y' → X'→ X` in place of `f`.

Gap filled: `lem:IV.1-localize-basic` states only the existence of an
isomorphism of the local rings; this statement is the canonical one. -/
@[blueprint "lem:IV.1-localize-basic-stalk"
  (statement := /-- Let $f\colon X'\to X$ be a morphism of schemes, $x$ a point of $X$, $S$ the
    local ring of $X$ at $x$, $Y'$ a subscheme of $X'$ and $Y'_S=Y'\times_X\operatorname{Spec}(S)$
    (\cref{lem:IV.1-localize-subscheme-product}). For every point $y$ of $Y'_S$, the canonical
    map from the local ring of $Y'$ at the image of $y$ to the local ring of $Y'_S$ at $y$,
    induced by the projection $Y'_S\to Y'$, is an isomorphism. (The canonical form of the
    assertion on the local rings, pp.~275--276.) -/)
  (proof := /-- The projection $Y'_S\to Y'$ is the base change of the canonical immersion
    $\operatorname{Spec}(S)\to X$ along $Y'\to X$. This immersion is flat, and so is its base
    change; its stalk maps are local and surjective, hence faithfully flat, hence injective, so
    bijective (the argument of \cref{lem:IV.1-localize-basic} applied to $Y'\to X'\to X$ in
    place of $f$). \textbf{Gap filled.} The paper says ``equal to (or, more precisely,
    canonically isomorphic to)''. -/)
  (latexEnv := "lemma")]
theorem Subscheme.stalkMap_localizeProj_bijective (Y' : Subscheme X')
    (y : (Y'.localize f x).toScheme) :
    Function.Bijective ((Subscheme.localizeProj f x Y').stalkMap y).hom := by
  unfold Subscheme.localizeProj
  rw [Scheme.Hom.stalkMap_comp]
  exact ((asIso (Scheme.Hom.stalkMap (Subscheme.localizeIso f x Y').hom y)).commRingCatIsoToRingEquiv.bijective).comp
    (stalkMap_localizeMap_bijective (Y'.ι ≫ f) x _)

end LocalizeCanonical

section SubschemeLocal

variable {Z : Scheme.{u}}

private theorem mem_pts_ι (D : Subscheme Z) (z : D.toScheme) : D.ι z ∈ D.pts := by
  show D.ι z ∈ (D.support : Set Z)
  rw [← Scheme.IdealSheafData.range_subschemeι]
  exact ⟨z, rfl⟩

private theorem exists_ι_eq_of_mem_pts (D : Subscheme Z) {z : Z} (hz : z ∈ D.pts) :
    ∃ z' : D.toScheme, D.ι z' = z := by
  have : z ∈ Set.range D.ι := by
    rw [Scheme.IdealSheafData.range_subschemeι]
    exact hz
  exact this

private theorem isReduced_stalk_quot (D : Subscheme Z) (hD : D.IsReduced) {z : Z} (hz : z ∈ D.pts) :
    _root_.IsReduced (Z.presheaf.stalk z ⧸ D.stalkIdeal z) := by
  have : IsReduced D.toScheme := hD
  obtain ⟨z', rfl⟩ := exists_ι_eq_of_mem_pts D hz
  obtain ⟨e⟩ := nonempty_stalk_quot_equiv D z'
  exact isReduced_of_injective e.toRingHom e.injective

private theorem isRegular_stalk_quot (D : Subscheme Z) (hD : D.IsNonsingular) {z : Z}
    (hz : z ∈ D.pts) : IsRegularLocalRing (Z.presheaf.stalk z ⧸ D.stalkIdeal z) := by
  obtain ⟨z', rfl⟩ := exists_ι_eq_of_mem_pts D hz
  obtain ⟨e⟩ := nonempty_stalk_quot_equiv D z'
  have : IsRegularLocalRing (D.toScheme.presheaf.stalk z') := hD z'
  exact IsRegularLocalRing.of_ringEquiv e.symm

private theorem isReduced_of_stalk_quot (D : Subscheme Z)
    (h : ∀ z ∈ D.pts, _root_.IsReduced (Z.presheaf.stalk z ⧸ D.stalkIdeal z)) :
    D.IsReduced := by
  have : ∀ z' : D.toScheme, _root_.IsReduced (D.toScheme.presheaf.stalk z') := fun z' => by
    obtain ⟨e⟩ := nonempty_stalk_quot_equiv D z'
    have := h (D.ι z') (mem_pts_ι D z')
    exact isReduced_of_injective e.symm.toRingHom e.symm.injective
  exact isReduced_of_isReduced_stalk _

private theorem isNonsingular_of_stalk_quot (D : Subscheme Z)
    (h : ∀ z ∈ D.pts, IsRegularLocalRing (Z.presheaf.stalk z ⧸ D.stalkIdeal z)) :
    D.IsNonsingular := fun z' => by
  obtain ⟨e⟩ := nonempty_stalk_quot_equiv D z'
  have := h (D.ι z') (mem_pts_ι D z')
  exact IsRegularLocalRing.of_ringEquiv e

private theorem isIrreducible_pts (D : Subscheme Z) (hD : D.IsIrreducible) :
    IsIrreducible D.pts := by
  have : IrreducibleSpace D.toScheme := hD
  have h := (IrreducibleSpace.isIrreducible_univ D.toScheme).image D.ι
    D.ι.continuous.continuousOn
  rwa [Set.image_univ, Scheme.IdealSheafData.range_subschemeι] at h

private theorem isIrreducible_of_pts (D : Subscheme Z) (h : IsIrreducible D.pts) :
    D.IsIrreducible := by
  have hr : IsIrreducible (Set.range D.ι) := by
    rw [Scheme.IdealSheafData.range_subschemeι]
    exact h
  have := Subtype.irreducibleSpace hr
  let e := D.ι.isEmbedding.toHomeomorph
  have h2 := (IrreducibleSpace.isIrreducible_univ (Set.range D.ι)).image e.symm
    e.symm.continuous.continuousOn
  rw [Set.image_univ, e.symm.surjective.range_eq] at h2
  exact (irreducibleSpace_def _).mpr h2

end SubschemeLocal

section LocalizeBasic

variable {X X' : Scheme.{u}} (f : X' ⟶ X) (x : X)

private theorem localize_isReduced (Y' : Subscheme X') (hY : Y'.IsReduced) :
    (Y'.localize f x).IsReduced := by
  refine isReduced_of_stalk_quot _ fun y hy => ?_
  have hjy : (localizeMap f x) y ∈ Y'.pts := by
    rw [pts_localize] at hy
    exact hy
  have e := Ideal.quotientEquiv (Y'.stalkIdeal ((localizeMap f x) y))
    ((Y'.localize f x).stalkIdeal y) (localizeStalkEquiv f x y) (stalkIdeal_localize f x Y' y)
  have := isReduced_stalk_quot Y' hY hjy
  exact isReduced_of_injective e.symm.toRingHom e.symm.injective

private theorem localize_isNonsingular (Y' : Subscheme X') (hY : Y'.IsNonsingular) :
    (Y'.localize f x).IsNonsingular := by
  refine isNonsingular_of_stalk_quot _ fun y hy => ?_
  have hjy : (localizeMap f x) y ∈ Y'.pts := by
    rw [pts_localize] at hy
    exact hy
  have e := Ideal.quotientEquiv (Y'.stalkIdeal ((localizeMap f x) y))
    ((Y'.localize f x).stalkIdeal y) (localizeStalkEquiv f x y) (stalkIdeal_localize f x Y' y)
  have := isRegular_stalk_quot Y' hY hjy
  exact IsRegularLocalRing.of_ringEquiv e

private theorem localize_empty_or_isIrreducible (Y' : Subscheme X') (hY : Y'.IsIrreducible) :
    Y'.localize f x = Subscheme.empty ∨ (Y'.localize f x).IsIrreducible := by
  by_cases hne : (Y'.localize f x).pts.Nonempty
  · right
    obtain ⟨y, hy⟩ := hne
    have hirr := isIrreducible_pts Y' hY
    have hcl : IsClosed Y'.pts := Y'.support.isClosed
    set η := hirr.genericPoint
    have hηspec : closure {η} = Y'.pts := by
      rw [hirr.isGenericPoint_genericPoint_closure.def, hcl.closure_eq]
    have hjy : (localizeMap f x) y ∈ Y'.pts := by
      rw [pts_localize] at hy
      exact hy
    have hηjy : η ⤳ (localizeMap f x) y :=
      specializes_iff_mem_closure.mpr (by rw [hηspec]; exact hjy)
    obtain ⟨η', hη'⟩ := mem_range_localizeMap_of_specializes f x hηjy ⟨y, rfl⟩
    have := isPreimmersion_localizeMap f x
    have hpts : (Y'.localize f x).pts = closure {η'} := by
      rw [pts_localize, (localizeMap f x).isEmbedding.isInducing.closure_eq_preimage_closure_image,
        Set.image_singleton, hη', hηspec]
    refine isIrreducible_of_pts _ ?_
    rw [hpts]
    exact isIrreducible_singleton.closure
  · left
    rw [Set.not_nonempty_iff_eq_empty] at hne
    refine (Scheme.IdealSheafData.support_eq_bot_iff (I := Y'.localize f x)).mp ?_
    ext1
    exact hne

end LocalizeBasic

section LocalizeSurj

variable {X X' : Scheme.{u}} (f : X' ⟶ X) (x : X)

private theorem fromSpecStalk_appLE {U : X.Opens} (hxU : x ∈ U) (h : ⊤ ≤ X.fromSpecStalk x ⁻¹ᵁ U) :
    (X.fromSpecStalk x).appLE U ⊤ h =
      X.presheaf.germ U x hxU ≫ (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (X.presheaf.stalk x)).inv := by
  rw [Scheme.Hom.appLE, Scheme.fromSpecStalk_app hxU]
  simp only [Category.assoc, ← Functor.map_comp]
  rw [show ((homOfLE le_top).op ≫ (homOfLE h).op :
      Opposite.op (⊤ : (Spec (X.presheaf.stalk x)).Opens) ⟶ Opposite.op ⊤) = 𝟙 _ from
    Subsingleton.elim _ _, CategoryTheory.Functor.map_id, Category.comp_id]

private theorem fromSpecStalk_le_preimage {U : X.Opens} (hxU : x ∈ U) :
    ⊤ ≤ X.fromSpecStalk x ⁻¹ᵁ U := fun p _ => by
  have : X.fromSpecStalk x p ∈ Set.range (X.fromSpecStalk x) := ⟨p, rfl⟩
  rw [Scheme.range_fromSpecStalk] at this
  exact this.mem_open U.isOpen hxU

private theorem quasiCompact_fromSpecStalk [IsAlgebraicScheme X] :
    QuasiCompact (X.fromSpecStalk x) := by
  have := IsAlgebraicScheme.isNoetherian X
  have : TopologicalSpace.NoetherianSpace (Spec (X.presheaf.stalk x)) :=
    inferInstanceAs (TopologicalSpace.NoetherianSpace (PrimeSpectrum (X.presheaf.stalk x)))
  exact ⟨fun _ _ _ => TopologicalSpace.NoetherianSpace.isCompact _⟩

private theorem quasiCompact_localizeMap [IsAlgebraicScheme X] :
    QuasiCompact (localizeMap f x) := by
  have := quasiCompact_fromSpecStalk x
  unfold localizeMap localizeScheme
  infer_instance

/-- Over an affine open `V ⊆ f⁻¹(U)` (`U` an affine neighbourhood of `x`), `j⁻¹(V)` is affine and
its ring of sections is a localization of `Γ(X', V)`. -/
private theorem localizeMap_preimage_affine {U : X.Opens} (hU : IsAffineOpen U) (hxU : x ∈ U)
    (V : X'.affineOpens) (hVU : (V : X'.Opens) ≤ f ⁻¹ᵁ U) :
    IsAffineOpen (localizeMap f x ⁻¹ᵁ V) ∧
      ∀ K : Ideal Γ(localizeScheme f x, localizeMap f x ⁻¹ᵁ V),
        (K.comap ((localizeMap f x).app V).hom).map ((localizeMap f x).app V).hom = K := by
  set j := localizeMap f x
  set g := X.fromSpecStalk x
  let π : localizeScheme f x ⟶ Spec (X.presheaf.stalk x) := pullback.snd f g
  have hgU := fromSpecStalk_le_preimage x hxU
  have H : IsPullback j π f g := IsPullback.of_hasPullback f g
  have hUY : j ⁻¹ᵁ (V : X'.Opens) = j ⁻¹ᵁ V ⊓ π ⁻¹ᵁ ⊤ := by
    rw [Scheme.Hom.preimage_top, inf_top_eq]
  have : IsAffine U := hU
  have : IsAffine (⊤ : (Spec (X.presheaf.stalk x)).Opens) := isAffineOpen_top _
  have : IsAffine (V : X'.Opens) := V.2
  have hUYaff : IsAffineOpen (j ⁻¹ᵁ (V : X'.Opens)) :=
    .of_isIso (Scheme.Hom.isPullback_resLE H hgU hVU hUY).isoPullback.hom
  refine ⟨hUYaff, ?_⟩
  have hiso := isIso_pushoutSection_of_isAffineOpen H hgU hVU hUY hU (isAffineOpen_top _) V.2
  have hpo := (isIso_pushoutSection_iff H hgU hVU hUY).mp hiso
  have h1 : j ⁻¹ᵁ (V : X'.Opens) ≤ j ⁻¹ᵁ (V : X'.Opens) := le_rfl
  have h2 : j ⁻¹ᵁ (V : X'.Opens) ≤ π ⁻¹ᵁ ⊤ := le_top
  let _ : Algebra Γ(X, U) Γ(X', V) := (f.appLE U V hVU).hom.toAlgebra
  let _ : Algebra Γ(X, U) Γ(Spec (X.presheaf.stalk x), ⊤) := (g.appLE U ⊤ hgU).hom.toAlgebra
  let _ : Algebra Γ(X', V) Γ(localizeScheme f x, j ⁻¹ᵁ (V : X'.Opens)) :=
    (j.appLE V (j ⁻¹ᵁ V) h1).hom.toAlgebra
  let _ : Algebra Γ(Spec (X.presheaf.stalk x), ⊤) Γ(localizeScheme f x, j ⁻¹ᵁ (V : X'.Opens)) :=
    (π.appLE ⊤ (j ⁻¹ᵁ V) h2).hom.toAlgebra
  let _ : Algebra Γ(X, U) Γ(localizeScheme f x, j ⁻¹ᵁ (V : X'.Opens)) :=
    (f.appLE U V hVU ≫ j.appLE V (j ⁻¹ᵁ V) h1).hom.toAlgebra
  have : IsScalarTower Γ(X, U) Γ(X', V) Γ(localizeScheme f x, j ⁻¹ᵁ (V : X'.Opens)) :=
    IsScalarTower.of_algebraMap_eq' rfl
  have : IsScalarTower Γ(X, U) Γ(Spec (X.presheaf.stalk x), ⊤)
      Γ(localizeScheme f x, j ⁻¹ᵁ (V : X'.Opens)) := IsScalarTower.of_algebraMap_eq' (by
    show (f.appLE U V hVU ≫ j.appLE V (j ⁻¹ᵁ V) h1).hom =
      (g.appLE U ⊤ hgU ≫ π.appLE ⊤ (j ⁻¹ᵁ V) h2).hom
    rw [hpo.w])
  have hA : Algebra.IsPushout Γ(X, U) Γ(X', V) Γ(Spec (X.presheaf.stalk x), ⊤)
      Γ(localizeScheme f x, j ⁻¹ᵁ (V : X'.Opens)) := CommRingCat.isPushout_iff_isPushout.mp hpo
  have hlocA : IsLocalization (hU.primeIdealOf ⟨x, hxU⟩).asIdeal.primeCompl
      Γ(Spec (X.presheaf.stalk x), ⊤) := by
    let _ := TopCat.Presheaf.algebra_section_stalk X.presheaf (U := U) ⟨x, hxU⟩
    have : IsLocalization (hU.primeIdealOf ⟨x, hxU⟩).asIdeal.primeCompl (X.presheaf.stalk x) :=
      hU.isLocalization_stalk ⟨x, hxU⟩
    let e : X.presheaf.stalk x ≃ₐ[Γ(X, U)] Γ(Spec (X.presheaf.stalk x), ⊤) :=
      { (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (X.presheaf.stalk x)).symm.commRingCatIsoToRingEquiv with
        commutes' := fun r => by
          show (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (X.presheaf.stalk x)).inv ((X.presheaf.germ U x hxU) r) =
            (g.appLE U ⊤ hgU) r
          rw [fromSpecStalk_appLE x hxU hgU]
          rfl }
    exact IsLocalization.isLocalization_of_algEquiv (hU.primeIdealOf ⟨x, hxU⟩).asIdeal.primeCompl e
  have hlocB := (Algebra.isLocalization_iff_isPushout (hU.primeIdealOf ⟨x, hxU⟩).asIdeal.primeCompl
    Γ(Spec (X.presheaf.stalk x), ⊤)).mpr hA
  intro K
  have key := IsLocalization.map_under
    (Algebra.algebraMapSubmonoid Γ(X', V) (hU.primeIdealOf ⟨x, hxU⟩).asIdeal.primeCompl)
    Γ(localizeScheme f x, j ⁻¹ᵁ (V : X'.Opens)) K
  rw [Scheme.Hom.app_eq_appLE]
  exact key

private theorem localize_surjective [IsAlgebraicScheme X] :
    Function.Surjective (Subscheme.localize f x) := by
  intro I
  have := quasiCompact_localizeMap f x
  refine ⟨I.map (localizeMap f x), ?_⟩
  obtain ⟨_, ⟨U, hU₀, rfl⟩, hxU, -⟩ :=
    X.isBasis_affineOpens.exists_subset_of_mem_open (Set.mem_univ x) isOpen_univ
  have hU : IsAffineOpen U := hU₀
  have hgU := fromSpecStalk_le_preimage x hxU
  have hloc := fun V : {V : X'.affineOpens // (V : X'.Opens) ≤ f ⁻¹ᵁ U} =>
    localizeMap_preimage_affine f x hU hxU V.1 V.2
  refine Scheme.IdealSheafData.ext_of_iSup_eq_top
    (fun V : {V : X'.affineOpens // (V : X'.Opens) ≤ f ⁻¹ᵁ U} =>
      (⟨localizeMap f x ⁻¹ᵁ V.1, (hloc V).1⟩ : (localizeScheme f x).affineOpens)) ?_ ?_
  · refine eq_top_iff.mpr fun y _ => ?_
    have hc : localizeMap f x ≫ f =
        (pullback.snd f (X.fromSpecStalk x) : localizeScheme f x ⟶ _) ≫ X.fromSpecStalk x :=
      pullback.condition
    have hy : (localizeMap f x) y ∈ f ⁻¹ᵁ U := by
      show f ((localizeMap f x) y) ∈ U
      rw [← Scheme.Hom.comp_apply, hc]
      exact hgU (Set.mem_univ ((pullback.snd f (X.fromSpecStalk x) : localizeScheme f x ⟶ _) y))
    obtain ⟨_, ⟨V, hV, rfl⟩, hyV, hVU⟩ :=
      X'.isBasis_affineOpens.exists_subset_of_mem_open hy (f ⁻¹ᵁ U).isOpen
    exact TopologicalSpace.Opens.mem_iSup.mpr ⟨⟨⟨V, hV⟩, hVU⟩, hyV⟩
  · intro V
    show ((I.map (localizeMap f x)).comap (localizeMap f x)).ideal _ = I.ideal _
    rw [ideal_comap_eq_map_appLE (localizeMap f x) (I.map (localizeMap f x)) V.1
      ⟨_, (hloc V).1⟩ le_rfl, Scheme.IdealSheafData.ideal_map I (localizeMap f x) V.1 (hloc V).1,
      ← Scheme.Hom.app_eq_appLE]
    exact (hloc V).2 _

private theorem isAlgebraicScheme_localizeScheme [Hironaka.Cited.ExistsFlatIsLocalHomAdicCompletionOfFlat.{u}] [Hironaka.Cited.ExistsSurjectiveMvPowerSeriesOfIsAdicComplete.{u}] [Hironaka.Cited.IsRegularLocalRingLocalizationIffRankJacobianEqHeight.{u}] [Hironaka.Cited.IsRegularLocalRingLocalizationOfIsRegularLocalRing.{u}] [Hironaka.Cited.IsRegularLocalRingOfFlatOfIsRegularLocalRing.{u}] [IsAlgebraicScheme X] [LocallyOfFiniteType f]
    [QuasiCompact f] : IsAlgebraicScheme (localizeScheme f x) := by
  obtain ⟨S, i1, i2, i3, p, hp, -⟩ := IsAlgebraicScheme.exists_base (X := X)
  obtain ⟨_, ⟨U, hU₀, rfl⟩, hxU, -⟩ :=
    X.isBasis_affineOpens.exists_subset_of_mem_open (Set.mem_univ x) isOpen_univ
  have hU : IsAffineOpen U := hU₀
  let φ : S →+* Γ(X, U) :=
    (p.appLE ⊤ U le_top).hom.comp (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of S)).inv.hom
  let _ : Algebra S Γ(X, U) := φ.toAlgebra
  have hφ : φ.FiniteType := by
    refine RingHom.FiniteType.comp ?_ (RingHom.FiniteType.of_surjective _ ?_)
    · exact HasRingHomProperty.appLE @LocallyOfFiniteType p hp ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top _⟩ ⟨U, hU⟩
        le_top
    · exact (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of S)).commRingCatIsoToRingEquiv.symm.surjective
  have : Algebra.FiniteType S Γ(X, U) := hφ
  have hB : IsHironakaBase (Localization.AtPrime (hU.primeIdealOf ⟨x, hxU⟩).asIdeal) :=
    IsHironakaBase.localization_atPrime_of_finiteType S Γ(X, U) (hU.primeIdealOf ⟨x, hxU⟩)
  let _ := TopCat.Presheaf.algebra_section_stalk X.presheaf (U := U) ⟨x, hxU⟩
  have : IsLocalization (hU.primeIdealOf ⟨x, hxU⟩).asIdeal.primeCompl (X.presheaf.stalk x) :=
    hU.isLocalization_stalk ⟨x, hxU⟩
  let e : Localization.AtPrime (hU.primeIdealOf ⟨x, hxU⟩).asIdeal ≃+* X.presheaf.stalk x :=
    (IsLocalization.algEquiv (hU.primeIdealOf ⟨x, hxU⟩).asIdeal.primeCompl _ _).toRingEquiv
  unfold localizeScheme
  exact ⟨⟨Localization.AtPrime (hU.primeIdealOf ⟨x, hxU⟩).asIdeal, inferInstance, inferInstance,
    hB, pullback.snd f (X.fromSpecStalk x) ≫ Spec.map e.toCommRingCatIso.hom,
    inferInstance, inferInstance⟩⟩

end LocalizeSurj

/-- The assertions of pp. 275–276 about the localization: `X'_S` is an algebraic scheme; the
canonical immersion `j` identifies it with the restriction of `X'` to `f⁻¹(Spec(S))`; every
subscheme of `X'_S` is induced by a subscheme of `X'`; the local ring of `Y'_S` at a point `y`
is canonically isomorphic to the local ring of `Y'` at `y`; and reducedness, non-singularity
and irreducibility are inherited by `Y'_S` from `Y'`.

Deviation from the paper (statement modified): "the local ring of `Y'_S` at `y` is equal to
the local ring of `Y'` at `y`" is stated here as the existence of a ring isomorphism between the
quotients of the stalks of the ambient schemes by the stalks of the ideal sheaves; the canonical
form (the stalk map of the projection `Y'_S → Y'` is bijective) is
`Subscheme.stalkMap_localizeProj_bijective` (node `lem:IV.1-localize-basic-stalk`), and the
isomorphism `Y'_S ≅ Y' ×_X Spec(S)` of p. 275 is `Subscheme.localizeIso` (node
`lem:IV.1-localize-subscheme-product`).

Formalization note (encoding): "irreducible" follows the paper's agreement that the empty
subscheme counts as irreducible (p. 163, p. 274): `Y'_S` may be empty (e.g. when `Y'` lies away
from `f⁻¹(Spec S)`), and Mathlib's `IrreducibleSpace` excludes the empty space, so the
conclusion reads "`Y'_S` is empty or irreducible".

Gap in the paper filled: the paper asserts these facts as obvious; in particular the
surjectivity of `Y' ↦ Y'_S` needs that `j⁻¹(V)` is affine with ring of sections a localization
of `Γ(X', V)` for affine `V` over an affine neighbourhood of `x`. -/
@[blueprint "lem:IV.1-localize-basic"
  (statement := /-- Let $f\colon X'\to X$ be a morphism of algebraic schemes of finite type,
    $x$ a point of $X$, $S$ the local ring of $X$ at $x$ and $j\colon X'_S\to X'$ the
    canonical immersion. Then: $X'_S$ is an algebraic scheme; $j$ identifies $X'_S$ with the
    restriction of $X'$ to the set of those points of $X'$ which belong to
    $f^{-1}(\operatorname{Spec}(S))$; every subscheme of $X'_S$ is induced by a subscheme of
    $X'$ (\cref{def:IV.1-localize-subscheme}); for every point $y$ of $Y'_S$, viewed also as a
    point of $Y'$, the local ring of $Y'_S$ at $y$ is canonically isomorphic to the local ring
    of $Y'$ at $y$; and if $Y'$ is reduced (resp.\ non-singular, resp.\ irreducible) then so
    is $Y'_S$. (pp.\ 275–276.)

    Formalization note (encoding): ``irreducible'' includes the empty subscheme, by the
    paper's agreement; the Lean statement says ``empty or irreducible''.

    \textbf{Deviation from the paper (statement modified).} The local rings of $Y'_S$ and $Y'$
    are asserted here to be isomorphic (the existence of an isomorphism of the quotients of the
    stalks); the canonical isomorphism is \cref{lem:IV.1-localize-basic-stalk}, and the isomorphism
    of $Y'_S$ with the product $Y'\times_X\operatorname{Spec}(S)$ is
    \cref{lem:IV.1-localize-subscheme-product}. -/)
  (proof := /-- The paper asserts these facts without proof, on the ground that $X'_S$ is the
    restriction of $X'$ to $f^{-1}(\operatorname{Spec}(S))$: $S$ belongs to the class
    $\mathfrak B$ and $\operatorname{Spec}(S)$ is an algebraic scheme, so the product
    $X'\times_X\operatorname{Spec}(S)$ of algebraic schemes is again one; the local rings are
    unchanged because $\operatorname{Spec}(S)\to X$ induces isomorphisms on the local rings at
    the points of its range; and reducedness, non-singularity and irreducibility are
    properties of the local rings, resp.\ (for irreducibility) are preserved because the
    points of $Y'_S$ are the generizations in $Y'$ of the points over $x$.

    \textbf{Gap in the paper filled.} The Lean proof shows that the stalk maps of $j$ are
    bijective ($j$ is flat with surjective local stalk maps, hence faithfully flat), and that
    every subscheme of $X'_S$ is induced, using that over an affine $V$ lying over an affine
    neighbourhood of $x$ the open $j^{-1}(V)$ is affine with ring of sections a localization of
    $\Gamma(X',V)$. -/)
  (latexEnv := "lemma")]
theorem isAlgebraicScheme_localizeScheme_and_isEmbedding_localizeMap [Hironaka.Cited.ExistsFlatIsLocalHomAdicCompletionOfFlat.{u}] [Hironaka.Cited.ExistsSurjectiveMvPowerSeriesOfIsAdicComplete.{u}] [Hironaka.Cited.IsRegularLocalRingLocalizationIffRankJacobianEqHeight.{u}] [Hironaka.Cited.IsRegularLocalRingLocalizationOfIsRegularLocalRing.{u}] [Hironaka.Cited.IsRegularLocalRingOfFlatOfIsRegularLocalRing.{u}] {X X' : Scheme.{u}} [IsAlgebraicScheme X] [IsAlgebraicScheme X']
    (f : X' ⟶ X) [LocallyOfFiniteType f] [QuasiCompact f] (x : X) :
    IsAlgebraicScheme (localizeScheme f x) ∧
    Topology.IsEmbedding (localizeMap f x).base ∧
    Set.range (localizeMap f x).base = f.base ⁻¹' {y : X | y ⤳ x} ∧
    Function.Surjective (Subscheme.localize f x) ∧
    (∀ y : localizeScheme f x,
      Nonempty ((localizeScheme f x).presheaf.stalk y ≃+*
        X'.presheaf.stalk ((localizeMap f x).base y))) ∧
    (∀ (Y' : Subscheme X') (y : localizeScheme f x),
      Nonempty (((localizeScheme f x).presheaf.stalk y ⧸ (Y'.localize f x).stalkIdeal y) ≃+*
        (X'.presheaf.stalk ((localizeMap f x).base y) ⧸
          Y'.stalkIdeal ((localizeMap f x).base y)))) ∧
    (∀ Y' : Subscheme X', Y'.IsReduced → (Y'.localize f x).IsReduced) ∧
    (∀ Y' : Subscheme X', Y'.IsNonsingular → (Y'.localize f x).IsNonsingular) ∧
    (∀ Y' : Subscheme X', Y'.IsIrreducible →
      Y'.localize f x = Subscheme.empty ∨ (Y'.localize f x).IsIrreducible) := by
  have := isPreimmersion_localizeMap f x
  exact ⟨isAlgebraicScheme_localizeScheme f x, (localizeMap f x).isEmbedding, range_localizeMap f x,
    localize_surjective f x, fun y => ⟨(localizeStalkEquiv f x y).symm⟩,
    fun Y' y => ⟨(Ideal.quotientEquiv _ _ (localizeStalkEquiv f x y)
      (stalkIdeal_localize f x Y' y)).symm⟩,
    fun Y' h => localize_isReduced f x Y' h, fun Y' h => localize_isNonsingular f x Y' h,
    fun Y' h => localize_empty_or_isIrreducible f x Y' h⟩

/-! ### Definition 1 (p. 276): the localized resolution datum `ℜ'_S` -/

/-- Definition 1 (I), p. 276.  If `ℜ' = (E'; V₁', …, V_β'; W')` is a datum of type `ℜ^{N,n}_I`
on `X'`, then `ℜ'_S = (E'_S; (V₁')_S, …, (V_β')_S; W'_S)`; for a datum with closed restriction
`F'` (resp. open restriction `U'`) the localization is `(ℜ'_S, F'_S)` (resp. `(ℜ'_S, U'_S)`),
`F'_S` being `Subscheme.localize` and `U'_S` being `localizeSet`.

Formalization note (encoding): the standing hypotheses of Definition 1 — `f` of finite type
and `X'` non-singular irreducible — are imposed in Remark 1 (`rem:IV.1-1`), not on the data;
`(E')_S` etc. are `Subscheme.localize` (total transforms along `j`). -/
@[blueprint "def:IV.1"
  (statement := /-- \textbf{Definition 1.} Let $f\colon X'\to X$ be a morphism of algebraic
    schemes which is of finite type. We assume that $X'$ is non-singular irreducible. Let
    $\mathfrak R'$ be a resolution datum (with or without restriction) on $X'$, $x$ a point of
    $X$ and $S$ the local ring of $X$ at $x$. Then we define and denote by $\mathfrak R'_S$
    (or $(\mathfrak R')_S$) the resolution datum on $X'_S$ induced by $\mathfrak R'$ as
    follows. (I) If $\mathfrak R'=(E';V_1',\dots,V_\beta';W')$, a resolution datum of type
    $\mathfrak R^{N,n}_{\mathrm I}$ on $X'$, then
    $\mathfrak R'_S=(E'_S;(V_1')_S,\dots,(V_\beta')_S;W'_S)$. If
    $\mathfrak R'=(\mathfrak R^{N,n}_{\mathrm I},F')$ (resp.\
    $=(\mathfrak R^{N,n}_{\mathrm I},U')$), a resolution datum of type
    $\mathfrak R^{N,n}_{\mathrm I}$ with closed restriction $F'$ (resp.\ open restriction
    $U'$), then $\mathfrak R'_S=((\mathfrak R^{N,n}_{\mathrm I})_S,F'_S)$ (resp.\
    $=((\mathfrak R^{N,n}_{\mathrm I})_S,U'_S)$). Part (II) is \cref{def:IV.1-II}.
    (p.\ 276.)

    Formalization note (encoding): the localized subschemes are the total transforms along
    $j\colon X'_S\to X'$ (\cref{def:IV.1-localize-subscheme}), $U'_S=j^{-1}(U')$, and the
    standing hypotheses ($f$ of finite type, $X'$ non-singular irreducible) are imposed in
    \cref{rem:IV.1-1} rather than in the definition. -/)
  (latexEnv := "definition")]
noncomputable def DatumI.Raw.localize {X X' : Scheme.{u}} (f : X' ⟶ X) (x : X)
    (ℜ : DatumI.Raw X') : DatumI.Raw (localizeScheme f x) where
  E := ℜ.E.localize f x
  β := ℜ.β
  V := fun j => (ℜ.V j).localize f x
  W := ℜ.W.localize f x

/-- Definition 1 (II), p. 276.  If `ℜ' = (E₁', …, E_α' | J', b | a₁, …, a_α)` is a datum of
type `ℜ^N_II` on `X'`, then `ℜ'_S = ((E₁')_S, …, (E_α')_S | J'_S, b | a₁, …, a_α)`, where
`J'_S` denotes the restriction of `J'` to `X'_S`, "which is a sheaf of non-zero ideals on
`X'_S`"; for a datum with closed restriction `F'` the localization is `(ℜ'_S, F'_S)`.

Formalization note (encoding): the restriction of the sheaf of ideals `J'` to `X'_S` is
realized, like every induced subscheme, as `Subscheme.localize`
(`def:IV.1-localize-subscheme`), i.e. as the total transform along the canonical immersion `j`;
the two agree because `j` is flat. -/
@[blueprint "def:IV.1-II"
  (statement := /-- \textbf{Definition 1 (II).} If
    $\mathfrak R'=\big(E_1',\dots,E_{\alpha}'\,\big|\,J',b\,\big|\,a_1,\dots,a_\alpha\big)$,
    a resolution datum of type $\mathfrak R^N_{\mathrm{II}}$ on $X'$, then
    $\mathfrak R'_S=\big((E_1')_S,\dots,(E_\alpha')_S\,\big|\,J'_S,b\,\big|\,
    a_1,\dots,a_\alpha\big)$, where $J'_S$ denotes the restriction of $J'$ to $X'_S$, which
    is a sheaf of non-zero ideals on $X'_S$. If $\mathfrak R'=(\mathfrak R^N_{\mathrm{II}},
    F')$, a resolution datum of type $\mathfrak R^N_{\mathrm{II}}$ with closed restriction
    $F'$, then $\mathfrak R'_S=((\mathfrak R^N_{\mathrm{II}})_S,F'_S)$. (p.\ 276.)

    Formalization note (encoding): $J'_S$ and the $(E_i')_S$ are total transforms along the
    flat canonical immersion $j\colon X'_S\to X'$ (\cref{def:IV.1-localize-subscheme}), which
    coincide with the restrictions of the sheaves of ideals. -/)
  (latexEnv := "definition")]
noncomputable def DatumII.Raw.localize {X X' : Scheme.{u}} (f : X' ⟶ X) (x : X)
    (ℜ : DatumII.Raw X') : DatumII.Raw (localizeScheme f x) where
  α := ℜ.α
  E := fun i => (ℜ.E i).localize f x
  a := ℜ.a
  J := ℜ.J.localize f x
  b := ℜ.b

/-! ### Remark 1 (p. 276) -/

section GeneralSubscheme

variable {Z : Scheme.{u}}

private theorem irreducibleComponents_congr {E₁ E₂ : Subscheme Z} (h : E₁.pts = E₂.pts) :
    E₁.irreducibleComponents = E₂.irreducibleComponents := by
  unfold Subscheme.irreducibleComponents
  rw [h]

private theorem hasOnlyNormalCrossingsWithAt_congr {E₁ E₂ : Subscheme Z} (h : E₁.pts = E₂.pts)
    (D : Subscheme Z) (z : Z) :
    E₁.HasOnlyNormalCrossingsWithAt D z ↔ E₂.HasOnlyNormalCrossingsWithAt D z := by
  unfold Subscheme.HasOnlyNormalCrossingsWithAt
  rw [irreducibleComponents_congr h]

private theorem mem_pts_iff_of_affine (D : Subscheme Z) {z : Z} {U : Z.affineOpens}
    (hzU : z ∈ (U : Z.Opens)) :
    z ∈ D.pts ↔ ∀ f ∈ D.ideal U, ¬ IsUnit (Z.presheaf.germ U z hzU f) := by
  show z ∈ (D.support : Set Z) ↔ _
  rw [SetLike.mem_coe, Scheme.IdealSheafData.mem_support_iff_of_mem (U := U) hzU,
    Scheme.mem_zeroLocus_iff]
  simp only [Scheme.mem_basicOpen _ _ _ hzU]
  rfl

private theorem pts_inf (A B : Subscheme Z) : (A ⊓ B).pts = A.pts ∪ B.pts := by
  ext z
  obtain ⟨_, ⟨U, hU, rfl⟩, hzU, -⟩ :=
    Z.isBasis_affineOpens.exists_subset_of_mem_open (Set.mem_univ z) isOpen_univ
  let U' : Z.affineOpens := ⟨U, hU⟩
  rw [Set.mem_union, mem_pts_iff_of_affine _ (U := U') hzU, mem_pts_iff_of_affine _ (U := U') hzU,
    mem_pts_iff_of_affine _ (U := U') hzU]
  constructor
  · intro h
    by_contra hne
    push Not at hne
    obtain ⟨⟨a, ha, hua⟩, ⟨b, hb, hub⟩⟩ := hne
    refine h (a * b) ⟨Ideal.mul_mem_right _ _ ha, Ideal.mul_mem_left _ _ hb⟩ ?_
    rw [map_mul]
    exact hua.mul hub
  · rintro (h | h) g hg
    · exact h g hg.1
    · exact h g hg.2

private theorem pts_iInf {α : ℕ} (E : Fin α → Subscheme Z) : (⨅ i, E i).pts = ⋃ i, (E i).pts := by
  classical
  ext z
  obtain ⟨_, ⟨U, hU, rfl⟩, hzU, -⟩ :=
    Z.isBasis_affineOpens.exists_subset_of_mem_open (Set.mem_univ z) isOpen_univ
  let U' : Z.affineOpens := ⟨U, hU⟩
  rw [Set.mem_iUnion, mem_pts_iff_of_affine _ (U := U') hzU]
  simp_rw [mem_pts_iff_of_affine _ (U := U') hzU]
  rw [Scheme.IdealSheafData.ideal_iInf, iInf_apply]
  constructor
  · intro h
    by_contra hne
    push Not at hne
    choose g hg hug using hne
    refine h (∏ i, g i) ((Submodule.mem_iInf _).mpr fun i => ?_) ?_
    · rw [← Finset.mul_prod_erase Finset.univ g (Finset.mem_univ i)]
      exact Ideal.mul_mem_right _ _ (hg i)
    · rw [map_prod, IsUnit.prod_univ_iff]
      exact hug
  · rintro ⟨i, hi⟩ g hg
    exact hi g ((Submodule.mem_iInf _).mp hg i)

/-- The ideal sheaf of a reduced subscheme is its own radical. -/
private theorem radical_eq_self_of_isReduced (D : Subscheme Z) (hD : D.IsReduced) :
    D.radical = D := by
  have : IsReduced D.toScheme := hD
  refine Scheme.IdealSheafData.ext (funext fun U => ?_)
  show (D.ideal U).radical = D.ideal U
  have e := (Scheme.IdealSheafData.subschemeObjIso D U).commRingCatIsoToRingEquiv
  have : _root_.IsReduced (Γ(Z, U) ⧸ D.ideal U) :=
    isReduced_of_injective e.symm.toRingHom e.symm.injective
  exact ((Ideal.isRadical_iff_quotient_reduced _).mpr this).radical

/-- A subscheme whose ideal sheaf is its own radical is reduced. -/
private theorem isReduced_of_radical_eq (D : Subscheme Z) (h : D.radical = D) : D.IsReduced := by
  refine isReduced_of_stalk_quot D fun z _ => ?_
  obtain ⟨_, ⟨U, hU₀, rfl⟩, hzU, -⟩ :=
    Z.isBasis_affineOpens.exists_subset_of_mem_open (Set.mem_univ z) isOpen_univ
  have hU : IsAffineOpen U := hU₀
  let _ := TopCat.Presheaf.algebra_section_stalk Z.presheaf (U := U) ⟨z, hzU⟩
  have : IsLocalization (hU.primeIdealOf ⟨z, hzU⟩).asIdeal.primeCompl (Z.presheaf.stalk z) :=
    hU.isLocalization_stalk ⟨z, hzU⟩
  have hrad : (D.ideal ⟨U, hU₀⟩).radical = D.ideal ⟨U, hU₀⟩ := by
    have := congrArg (fun I => Scheme.IdealSheafData.ideal I ⟨U, hU₀⟩) h
    exact this
  rw [stalkIdeal_eq_map_germ D ⟨U, hU₀⟩ hzU]
  refine (Ideal.isRadical_iff_quotient_reduced _).mp ?_
  have := IsLocalization.map_radical (hU.primeIdealOf ⟨z, hzU⟩).asIdeal.primeCompl
    (Z.presheaf.stalk z) (D.ideal ⟨U, hU₀⟩)
  rw [hrad] at this
  show ((D.ideal ⟨U, hU₀⟩).map (algebraMap Γ(Z, U) (Z.presheaf.stalk z))).IsRadical
  rw [Ideal.IsRadical, ← this]

private theorem pts_ofClosed (T : Closeds Z) : (Subscheme.ofClosed T).pts = T :=
  Scheme.IdealSheafData.coe_support_vanishingIdeal T

private theorem ofClosed_radical (T : Closeds Z) :
    (Subscheme.ofClosed T).radical = Subscheme.ofClosed T := by
  have h1 : (Subscheme.ofClosed T).support = T := by
    ext1
    exact Scheme.IdealSheafData.coe_support_vanishingIdeal T
  have := Scheme.IdealSheafData.vanishingIdeal_support (I := Subscheme.ofClosed T)
  rw [h1] at this
  exact this.symm

private theorem ofClosed_isReduced (T : Closeds Z) : (Subscheme.ofClosed T).IsReduced :=
  isReduced_of_radical_eq _ (ofClosed_radical T)

/-- A reduced subscheme is the reduced subscheme on its support. -/
private theorem eq_ofClosed_support (D : Subscheme Z) (hD : D.IsReduced) :
    D = Subscheme.ofClosed D.support := by
  unfold Subscheme.ofClosed
  rw [Scheme.IdealSheafData.vanishingIdeal_support, radical_eq_self_of_isReduced D hD]

end GeneralSubscheme

section NormalFlat

variable {Z : Scheme.{u}}

/-- `V` is normally flat along `W ⊆ V` at `x` iff `O_{V,x} = O_{Z,x}/V_x` is normally flat along
the image of `W_x`. -/
private theorem isNormallyFlatAlongAt'_iff (V W : Subscheme Z) (hWV : W.IsContainedIn V) (z : Z) :
    Subscheme.IsNormallyFlatAlongAt' V W z ↔ z ∈ W.pts ∧
      IsNormallyFlatAlongIdeal ((W.stalkIdeal z).map (Ideal.Quotient.mk (V.stalkIdeal z))) := by
  have key : ∀ z' : V.toScheme,
      (Subscheme.totalTransform V.ι W).stalkIdeal z' =
        ((W.stalkIdeal (V.ι z')).map (Ideal.Quotient.mk (V.stalkIdeal (V.ι z')))).map
          ((Ideal.quotEquivOfEq (stalkIdeal_eq_ker_stalkMap V z')).trans
            (RingHom.quotientKerEquivOfSurjective (V.ι.stalkMap_surjective z'))
            : _ →+* V.toScheme.presheaf.stalk z') := by
    intro z'
    rw [stalkIdeal_totalTransform, Ideal.map_map]
    rfl
  have hpts : ∀ z' : V.toScheme, z' ∈ (Subscheme.totalTransform V.ι W).pts ↔ V.ι z' ∈ W.pts := by
    intro z'
    change z' ∈ ((W.comap V.ι).support : Set V.toScheme) ↔ _
    rw [Scheme.IdealSheafData.support_comap]
    rfl
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨z', rfl, hz'1, hz'2⟩
    refine ⟨(hpts z').mp hz'1, ?_⟩
    rw [key] at hz'2
    let ψ := (Ideal.quotEquivOfEq (stalkIdeal_eq_ker_stalkMap V z')).trans
        (RingHom.quotientKerEquivOfSurjective (V.ι.stalkMap_surjective z'))
    refine isNormallyFlatAlongIdeal_of_ringEquiv ψ.symm _ _ ?_ hz'2
    rw [Ideal.map_map]
    convert Ideal.map_id _
    ext a
    simp only [RingHom.coe_comp, Function.comp_apply, RingHom.id_apply]
    rw [RingEquiv.coe_toRingHom, RingEquiv.symm_apply_eq]
    rfl
  · rintro ⟨hzW, hnf⟩
    obtain ⟨z', rfl⟩ := exists_ι_eq_of_mem_pts V (pts_subset_of_isContainedIn hWV hzW)
    refine ⟨z', rfl, (hpts z').mpr hzW, ?_⟩
    rw [key]
    exact isNormallyFlatAlongIdeal_of_ringEquiv _ _ _ rfl hnf

end NormalFlat

section Codim

variable {Z : Scheme.{u}}

/-- The local ring of `Z` at the generic point `ξ` of `W` is `(O_{Z,x})_{W_x}` for `x ∈ W`
(when `W_x` is prime).  (Same argument as in Ch. II §1.) -/
private theorem nonempty_stalk_equiv_localization' {X : Scheme.{u}} (W : Subscheme X)
    {ξ : X} (hξ : IsGenericPoint ξ W.pts) {x : X} (hx : x ∈ W.pts)
    [hq : (W.stalkIdeal x).IsPrime] :
    Nonempty (X.presheaf.stalk ξ ≃+* Localization.AtPrime (W.stalkIdeal x)) := by
  have hspec : ξ ⤳ x := by
    rw [specializes_iff_mem_closure, hξ.def]
    exact hx
  obtain ⟨_, ⟨U, hU₀, rfl⟩, hxU, -⟩ :=
    X.isBasis_affineOpens.exists_subset_of_mem_open (Set.mem_univ x) isOpen_univ
  have hU : IsAffineOpen U := hU₀
  have hξU : ξ ∈ U := hspec.mem_open U.isOpen hxU
  have hxr : x ∈ Set.range hU.fromSpec := by rw [hU.range_fromSpec]; exact hxU
  have hξr : ξ ∈ Set.range hU.fromSpec := by rw [hU.range_fromSpec]; exact hξU
  obtain ⟨px, rfl⟩ := hxr
  obtain ⟨pξ, rfl⟩ := hξr
  have hle : pξ.asIdeal ≤ px.asIdeal :=
    (PrimeSpectrum.le_iff_specializes (x := pξ) (y := px)).mpr
      ((hU.fromSpec.isOpenEmbedding.isInducing.specializes_iff).mp hspec)
  let _ : Algebra Γ(X, U) (X.presheaf.stalk (hU.fromSpec px)) :=
    TopCat.Presheaf.algebra_section_stalk X.presheaf ⟨hU.fromSpec px, hxU⟩
  have hpx : px.asIdeal.IsPrime := PrimeSpectrum.isPrime px
  have hpξ : pξ.asIdeal.IsPrime := PrimeSpectrum.isPrime pξ
  have hlocx : IsLocalization.AtPrime (X.presheaf.stalk (hU.fromSpec px)) px.asIdeal :=
    hU.isLocalization_stalk' px hxU
  set I := W.ideal ⟨U, hU₀⟩ with hI
  -- the stalk `W_x` is generated by `W(U)`
  have hW : W.stalkIdeal (hU.fromSpec px) =
      I.map (algebraMap Γ(X, U) (X.presheaf.stalk (hU.fromSpec px))) := by
    apply le_antisymm
    · rw [Subscheme.stalkIdeal, Ideal.span_le]
      rintro _ ⟨V, hxV, s, hs, rfl⟩
      obtain ⟨_, ⟨D, hD, rfl⟩, hxD, hDUV⟩ := X.isBasis_affineOpens.exists_subset_of_mem_open
        (show hU.fromSpec px ∈ (U ⊓ V.1 : TopologicalSpace.Opens X) from ⟨hxU, hxV⟩)
        (U ⊓ V.1).isOpen
      have hDV : (⟨D, hD⟩ : X.affineOpens) ≤ V := hDUV.trans inf_le_right
      have hDU : (⟨D, hD⟩ : X.affineOpens) ≤ ⟨U, hU₀⟩ := hDUV.trans inf_le_left
      have h1 := W.ideal_le_comap_ideal hDV hs
      rw [Ideal.mem_comap, ← W.map_ideal hDU] at h1
      have h2 := Ideal.mem_map_of_mem (X.presheaf.germ D _ hxD).hom h1
      rw [Ideal.map_map] at h2
      have e1 : (X.presheaf.germ D _ hxD).hom.comp
          (X.presheaf.map (CategoryTheory.homOfLE hDU).op).hom =
          algebraMap Γ(X, U) (X.presheaf.stalk (hU.fromSpec px)) := by
        ext t
        exact X.presheaf.germ_res_apply (CategoryTheory.homOfLE hDU) _ hxD t
      have e2 : (X.presheaf.germ D _ hxD).hom
          ((X.presheaf.map (CategoryTheory.homOfLE hDV).op).hom s) =
          (X.presheaf.germ V.1 _ hxV).hom s := X.presheaf.germ_res_apply _ _ _ _
      rw [e1, e2] at h2
      exact h2
    · rw [Ideal.map_le_iff_le_comap]
      intro t ht
      exact Ideal.subset_span ⟨⟨U, hU₀⟩, hxU, t, ht, rfl⟩
  -- `√W(U) = P_ξ`: `V(W(U)) = W ∩ U = closure {ξ} ∩ U`
  have hzero : PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus (I : Set Γ(X, U)) =
      PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus (pξ.asIdeal : Set Γ(X, U)) := by
    ext p
    have h1 : hU.fromSpec '' PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus (I : Set Γ(X, U)) =
        (W.support : Set X) ∩ U := by
      rw [hU.fromSpec_image_zeroLocus, W.coe_support_inter ⟨U, hU₀⟩]
    have h2 : p ∈ PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus (I : Set Γ(X, U)) ↔ hU.fromSpec p ∈ W.pts := by
      constructor
      · intro hp
        have : hU.fromSpec p ∈ hU.fromSpec '' PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus (I : Set Γ(X, U)) :=
          ⟨p, hp, rfl⟩
        rw [h1] at this
        exact this.1
      · intro hp
        have : hU.fromSpec p ∈ (W.support : Set X) ∩ U :=
          ⟨hp, by rw [← hU.range_fromSpec]; exact ⟨p, rfl⟩⟩
        rw [← h1] at this
        obtain ⟨p', hp', he⟩ := this
        rwa [← hU.fromSpec.isOpenEmbedding.injective he]
    have h3 : hU.fromSpec p ∈ W.pts ↔ pξ.asIdeal ≤ p.asIdeal := by
      rw [← hξ.def, ← specializes_iff_mem_closure]
      refine hU.fromSpec.isOpenEmbedding.isInducing.specializes_iff.trans ?_
      exact (PrimeSpectrum.le_iff_specializes (x := pξ) (y := p)).symm
    rw [h2, h3, PrimeSpectrum.mem_zeroLocus]
    exact SetLike.coe_subset_coe.symm
  have hrad : I.radical = pξ.asIdeal := by
    rw [← PrimeSpectrum.vanishingIdeal_zeroLocus_eq_radical, hzero,
      PrimeSpectrum.vanishingIdeal_zeroLocus_eq_radical, hpξ.radical]
  -- `W_x = P_ξ O_{X,x}`
  have hq' : W.stalkIdeal (hU.fromSpec px) =
      pξ.asIdeal.map (algebraMap Γ(X, U) (X.presheaf.stalk (hU.fromSpec px))) := by
    apply le_antisymm
    · rw [hW]
      exact Ideal.map_mono (hrad ▸ Ideal.le_radical)
    · rw [Ideal.map_le_iff_le_comap]
      intro a ha
      rw [← hrad] at ha
      obtain ⟨n, hn⟩ := ha
      have := Ideal.mem_map_of_mem (algebraMap Γ(X, U) (X.presheaf.stalk (hU.fromSpec px))) hn
      rw [← hW, map_pow] at this
      exact hq.mem_of_pow_mem n this
  have hcomap : (W.stalkIdeal (hU.fromSpec px)).comap
      (algebraMap Γ(X, U) (X.presheaf.stalk (hU.fromSpec px))) = pξ.asIdeal := by
    rw [hq']
    exact IsLocalization.under_map_of_isPrime_disjoint px.asIdeal.primeCompl _ hpξ
      (by
        rw [Set.disjoint_left]
        intro a ha ha'
        exact ha (hle ha'))
  have hlocq : IsLocalization.AtPrime (Localization.AtPrime (W.stalkIdeal (hU.fromSpec px)))
      pξ.asIdeal := by
    have := IsLocalization.isLocalization_isLocalization_atPrime_isLocalization
      px.asIdeal.primeCompl
      (S := X.presheaf.stalk (hU.fromSpec px))
      (Localization.AtPrime (W.stalkIdeal (hU.fromSpec px))) (W.stalkIdeal (hU.fromSpec px))
    convert this using 2
    exact hcomap.symm
  let _ : Algebra Γ(X, U) (X.presheaf.stalk (hU.fromSpec pξ)) :=
    TopCat.Presheaf.algebra_section_stalk X.presheaf ⟨hU.fromSpec pξ, hξU⟩
  have hlocξ : IsLocalization.AtPrime (X.presheaf.stalk (hU.fromSpec pξ)) pξ.asIdeal :=
    hU.isLocalization_stalk' pξ hξU
  exact ⟨(IsLocalization.algEquiv pξ.asIdeal.primeCompl (X.presheaf.stalk (hU.fromSpec pξ))
    (Localization.AtPrime (W.stalkIdeal (hU.fromSpec px)))).toRingEquiv⟩

private theorem isPrime_stalkIdeal_of_isNonsingular (W : Subscheme Z) (hW : W.IsNonsingular) {z : Z}
    (hz : z ∈ W.pts) : (W.stalkIdeal z).IsPrime := by
  have := isRegular_stalk_quot W hW hz
  have := isDomain_of_isRegularLocalRing (Z.presheaf.stalk z ⧸ W.stalkIdeal z)
  exact (Ideal.Quotient.isDomain_iff_prime _).mp this

/-- Along a non-singular subscheme `W` with generic point `ξ`, the height of `W_z` is the
dimension of `O_{Z,ξ}`. -/
private theorem height_stalkIdeal_eq (W : Subscheme Z) (hW : W.IsNonsingular) {ξ : Z}
    (hξ : IsGenericPoint ξ W.pts) {z : Z} (hz : z ∈ W.pts) :
    ((W.stalkIdeal z).height : WithBot ℕ∞) = ringKrullDim (Z.presheaf.stalk ξ) := by
  have := isPrime_stalkIdeal_of_isNonsingular W hW hz
  obtain ⟨e⟩ := nonempty_stalk_equiv_localization' W hξ hz
  rw [ringKrullDim_eq_of_ringEquiv e,
    IsLocalization.AtPrime.ringKrullDim_eq_height (W.stalkIdeal z)]

/-- The codimension of a non-singular irreducible subscheme is the height at any of its
points. -/
private theorem codim_eq_height (W : Subscheme Z) (hW : W.IsNonsingular) (hirr : W.IsIrreducible)
    {z : Z} (hz : z ∈ W.pts) : W.codim = (W.stalkIdeal z).height := by
  have hI := isIrreducible_pts W hirr
  obtain ⟨ξ, hξ⟩ : ∃ ξ, IsGenericPoint ξ W.pts := QuasiSober.sober hI W.support.isClosed
  have hc : ∀ w ∈ W.pts, (W.stalkIdeal w).height = (W.stalkIdeal z).height := by
    intro w hw
    have h1 := height_stalkIdeal_eq W hW hξ hw
    have h2 := height_stalkIdeal_eq W hW hξ hz
    exact_mod_cast h1.trans h2.symm
  refine le_antisymm (iInf₂_le z hz) (le_iInf₂ fun w hw => ?_)
  exact (hc w hw).ge

end Codim

section LocalizeDatum

variable {X X' : Scheme.{u}} (f : X' ⟶ X) (x : X)

private theorem localize_codimAt (D : Subscheme X') (y : localizeScheme f x) :
    (D.localize f x).codimAt y = D.codimAt ((localizeMap f x) y) := by
  unfold Subscheme.codimAt
  rw [stalkIdeal_localize, RingEquiv.height_map]

private theorem localize_bot : (⊥ : Subscheme X').localize f x = ⊥ :=
  Scheme.IdealSheafData.comap_bot _

private theorem localize_top : (⊤ : Subscheme X').localize f x = ⊤ :=
  Scheme.IdealSheafData.comap_top _

private theorem localize_mono {D D' : Subscheme X'} (h : D ≤ D') :
    D.localize f x ≤ D'.localize f x :=
  Scheme.IdealSheafData.comap_mono _ h

/-- The irreducible components of `E'_S` through `y` are the localizations of the irreducible
components of `E'` through `j y`. -/
private theorem localize_irreducibleComponents (E : Subscheme X')
    {C' : Subscheme (localizeScheme f x)}
    (hC' : C' ∈ (E.localize f x).irreducibleComponents) {y : localizeScheme f x}
    (hy : y ∈ C'.pts) :
    ∃ C ∈ E.irreducibleComponents, (localizeMap f x) y ∈ C.pts ∧ C' = C.localize f x := by
  have := isPreimmersion_localizeMap f x
  have hemb := (localizeMap f x).isEmbedding
  obtain ⟨ZS, ⟨⟨hZirr, hZsub⟩, hZmax⟩, rfl⟩ := hC'
  set ζ' := hZirr.genericPoint
  have hζ'spec : closure {ζ'} = (ZS : Set _) := by
    rw [hZirr.isGenericPoint_genericPoint_closure.def, ZS.isClosed.closure_eq]
  set ζ := (localizeMap f x) ζ'
  let Zc : Closeds X' := ⟨closure {ζ}, isClosed_closure⟩
  have hZS : (ZS : Set _) = (localizeMap f x).base ⁻¹' closure {ζ} := by
    rw [← hζ'spec, hemb.isInducing.closure_eq_preimage_closure_image, Set.image_singleton]
  have hζE : ζ ∈ E.pts := by
    have : ζ' ∈ (E.localize f x).pts := hZsub (by rw [← hζ'spec]; exact subset_closure rfl)
    rw [pts_localize] at this
    exact this
  have hZE : (Zc : Set X') ⊆ E.pts :=
    closure_minimal (Set.singleton_subset_iff.mpr hζE) E.support.isClosed
  have hmax : Maximal (fun T : Closeds X' => IsIrreducible (T : Set X') ∧ (T : Set X') ⊆ E.pts)
      Zc := by
    refine ⟨⟨isIrreducible_singleton.closure, hZE⟩, fun T ⟨hTirr, hTE⟩ hZT => ?_⟩
    obtain ⟨τ, hτ⟩ : ∃ τ, IsGenericPoint τ (T : Set X') := QuasiSober.sober hTirr T.isClosed
    have hτζ : τ ⤳ ζ := by
      rw [specializes_iff_mem_closure, hτ.def]
      exact hZT (subset_closure rfl)
    obtain ⟨τ', hτ'⟩ := mem_range_localizeMap_of_specializes f x hτζ ⟨ζ', rfl⟩
    let TS : Closeds (localizeScheme f x) :=
      ⟨(localizeMap f x).base ⁻¹' T, T.isClosed.preimage (localizeMap f x).base.hom.continuous⟩
    have hTS : (TS : Set _) = closure {τ'} := by
      show (localizeMap f x).base ⁻¹' T = _
      rw [hemb.isInducing.closure_eq_preimage_closure_image, Set.image_singleton, hτ', hτ.def]
    have hle : ZS ≤ TS := by
      intro w hw
      rw [← SetLike.mem_coe, hZS] at hw
      exact hZT hw
    have hTSle : TS ≤ ZS := hZmax (y := TS) ⟨by rw [hTS]; exact isIrreducible_singleton.closure,
      fun w hw => by
        rw [pts_localize]
        exact hTE hw⟩ hle
    have hτ'Z : τ' ∈ (ZS : Set _) :=
      hTSle (by rw [← SetLike.mem_coe, hTS]; exact subset_closure rfl)
    rw [hZS] at hτ'Z
    have : τ ∈ closure {ζ} := by rw [← hτ']; exact hτ'Z
    intro w hw
    rw [← SetLike.mem_coe, ← hτ.def] at hw
    exact closure_minimal (Set.singleton_subset_iff.mpr this) isClosed_closure hw
  have hyZ : (localizeMap f x) y ∈ closure {ζ} := by
    have : y ∈ (ZS : Set _) := by
      rw [← pts_ofClosed ZS]
      exact hy
    rw [hZS] at this
    exact this
  refine ⟨Subscheme.ofClosed Zc, ⟨Zc, hmax, rfl⟩, ?_, ?_⟩
  · rw [pts_ofClosed]
    exact hyZ
  · have hred := localize_isReduced f x _ (ofClosed_isReduced Zc)
    rw [eq_ofClosed_support _ hred]
    congr 1
    ext1
    change (ZS : Set _) = ((Subscheme.ofClosed Zc).localize f x).pts
    rw [pts_localize, pts_ofClosed, hZS]
    rfl

/-- Normal crossings are inherited by the localization. -/
private theorem localize_hasOnlyNormalCrossingsWithAt (E D : Subscheme X') (y : localizeScheme f x)
    (h : E.HasOnlyNormalCrossingsWithAt D ((localizeMap f x) y)) :
    (E.localize f x).HasOnlyNormalCrossingsWithAt (D.localize f x) y := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨z, hz, hcomp, t, htz, hDt⟩ := h
  set e := localizeStalkEquiv f x y
  have hmapset : ∀ s : Finset (X'.presheaf.stalk ((localizeMap f x) y)),
      ((s.map e.toEquiv.toEmbedding : Finset _) : Set _) = e '' (s : Set _) := by
    intro s
    simp
  refine ⟨z.map e.toEquiv.toEmbedding, ⟨?_, ?_⟩, fun C' hC' hyC' => ?_, t.map e.toEquiv.toEmbedding,
    Finset.map_subset_map.mpr htz, ?_⟩
  · rw [hmapset, ← Ideal.map_span, hz.1]
    exact IsLocalRing.map_ringEquiv_maximalIdeal e
  · rw [Finset.card_map, hz.2]
    exact ringKrullDim_eq_of_ringEquiv e
  · obtain ⟨C, hC, hjC, rfl⟩ := localize_irreducibleComponents f x E hC' hyC'
    obtain ⟨a, haz, hCa⟩ := hcomp C hC hjC
    refine ⟨e a, Finset.mem_map_of_mem _ haz, ?_⟩
    rw [stalkIdeal_localize, hCa, Ideal.map_span, Set.image_singleton]
  · rw [stalkIdeal_localize, hDt, Ideal.map_span, hmapset]

private theorem localize_isNonsingularIrreducibleCodimOne (F : Subscheme X')
    (hF : F.IsNonsingularIrreducibleCodimOne) :
    (F.localize f x).IsNonsingularIrreducibleCodimOne := by
  rcases hF with h | ⟨hns, hirr, hcodim⟩
  · left
    rw [h]
    exact localize_top f x
  · rcases localize_empty_or_isIrreducible f x F hirr with h | h
    · exact Or.inl h
    · right
      have hns' := localize_isNonsingular f x F hns
      refine ⟨hns', h, ?_⟩
      obtain ⟨y, hy⟩ : (F.localize f x).pts.Nonempty := (isIrreducible_pts _ h).nonempty
      have hjy : (localizeMap f x) y ∈ F.pts := by
        rw [pts_localize] at hy
        exact hy
      rw [codim_eq_height _ hns' h hy, stalkIdeal_localize, RingEquiv.height_map,
        ← codim_eq_height F hns hirr hjy, hcodim]

/-- Density along the localization: a point of `X'_S` whose image lies in the closure of a
locally closed set `O ∩ C` of `X'` lies in the closure of the preimage. -/
private theorem mem_closure_preimage [IsAlgebraicScheme X'] {O C : Set X'} (hO : IsOpen O)
    (hC : IsClosed C) {y : localizeScheme f x} (hy : (localizeMap f x) y ∈ closure (O ∩ C)) :
    y ∈ closure ((localizeMap f x).base ⁻¹' (O ∩ C)) := by
  classical
  have := isPreimmersion_localizeMap f x
  have hemb := (localizeMap f x).isEmbedding
  rw [hemb.isInducing.closure_eq_preimage_closure_image, Set.image_preimage_eq_inter_range]
  show (localizeMap f x) y ∈ closure (O ∩ C ∩ Set.range (localizeMap f x).base)
  have := IsAlgebraicScheme.noetherianSpace X'
  obtain ⟨S, hSirr, hSeq⟩ := TopologicalSpace.NoetherianSpace.exists_finset_irreducible
    (⟨closure (O ∩ C), isClosed_closure⟩ : Closeds X')
  have hcl : closure (O ∩ C) = ⋃ K ∈ S, (K : Set X') := by
    have := congrArg (fun T : Closeds X' => (T : Set X')) hSeq
    simpa [TopologicalSpace.Closeds.coe_finset_sup] using this
  set S' := S.filter fun K : Closeds X' => ((K : Set X') ∩ O).Nonempty
  have hsub : closure (O ∩ C) ⊆ ⋃ K ∈ S', (K : Set X') := by
    refine closure_minimal (fun a ha => ?_) ?_
    · have : a ∈ ⋃ K ∈ S, (K : Set X') := hcl ▸ subset_closure ha
      obtain ⟨K, hK, haK⟩ := Set.mem_iUnion₂.mp this
      exact Set.mem_iUnion₂.mpr ⟨K, Finset.mem_filter.mpr ⟨hK, a, haK, ha.1⟩, haK⟩
    · exact S'.finite_toSet.isClosed_biUnion fun K _ => K.isClosed
  obtain ⟨K, hK, hyK⟩ := Set.mem_iUnion₂.mp (hsub hy)
  obtain ⟨hKS, hKO⟩ := Finset.mem_filter.mp hK
  obtain ⟨κ, hκ⟩ : ∃ κ, IsGenericPoint κ (K : Set X') :=
    QuasiSober.sober (hSirr ⟨K, hKS⟩) K.isClosed
  have hκO : κ ∈ O := (hκ.mem_open_set_iff hO).mpr hKO
  have hκC : κ ∈ C := by
    have hKcl : (K : Set X') ⊆ closure (O ∩ C) := by
      rw [hcl]
      exact Set.subset_biUnion_of_mem (u := fun K : Closeds X' => (K : Set X')) hKS
    exact closure_minimal Set.inter_subset_right hC (hKcl hκ.mem)
  have hκy : κ ⤳ (localizeMap f x) y := hκ.specializes hyK
  have hκr := mem_range_localizeMap_of_specializes f x hκy ⟨y, rfl⟩
  exact closure_mono (Set.singleton_subset_iff.mpr
    (show κ ∈ O ∩ C ∩ Set.range (localizeMap f x).base from ⟨⟨hκO, hκC⟩, hκr⟩))
    (specializes_iff_mem_closure.mp hκy)

private theorem localize_isNormallyFlatAlongAt' (V W : Subscheme X') (hWV : W.IsContainedIn V)
    (y : localizeScheme f x)
    (h : Subscheme.IsNormallyFlatAlongAt' V W ((localizeMap f x) y)) :
    Subscheme.IsNormallyFlatAlongAt' (V.localize f x) (W.localize f x) y := by
  have hWV' : (W.localize f x).IsContainedIn (V.localize f x) :=
    fun U => localize_mono f x (fun U => hWV U) U
  rw [isNormallyFlatAlongAt'_iff _ _ hWV] at h
  rw [isNormallyFlatAlongAt'_iff _ _ hWV']
  obtain ⟨hyW, hnf⟩ := h
  refine ⟨by rw [pts_localize]; exact hyW, ?_⟩
  let ē := Ideal.quotientEquiv (V.stalkIdeal ((localizeMap f x) y))
    ((V.localize f x).stalkIdeal y) (localizeStalkEquiv f x y) (stalkIdeal_localize f x V y)
  refine isNormallyFlatAlongIdeal_of_ringEquiv ē _ _ ?_ hnf
  rw [Ideal.map_map, stalkIdeal_localize f x W y, ← Ideal.map_coe (localizeStalkEquiv f x y),
    Ideal.map_map]
  rfl

private theorem localize_isSimpleAt (W : Subscheme X') (y : localizeScheme f x)
    (h : W.IsSimpleAt ((localizeMap f x) y)) : (W.localize f x).IsSimpleAt y := by
  obtain ⟨hyW, hreg⟩ := h
  refine ⟨by rw [pts_localize]; exact hyW, ?_⟩
  have e := Ideal.quotientEquiv (W.stalkIdeal ((localizeMap f x) y))
    ((W.localize f x).stalkIdeal y) (localizeStalkEquiv f x y) (stalkIdeal_localize f x W y)
  exact IsRegularLocalRing.of_ringEquiv e

private theorem localize_stalkIdeal_ne_bot (J : Subscheme X') (y : localizeScheme f x)
    (h : J.stalkIdeal ((localizeMap f x) y) ≠ ⊥) : (J.localize f x).stalkIdeal y ≠ ⊥ := by
  rw [stalkIdeal_localize]
  intro h'
  exact h ((Ideal.map_eq_bot_iff_of_injective (localizeStalkEquiv f x y).injective).mp h')

private theorem localize_pts_inf (A B : Subscheme X') :
    ((A.localize f x).union (B.localize f x)).pts = ((A.union B).localize f x).pts := by
  unfold Subscheme.union
  rw [pts_inf, pts_localize, pts_localize, pts_localize, pts_inf, Set.preimage_union]

private theorem localize_pts_iInf {α : ℕ} (E : Fin α → Subscheme X') :
    (⨅ i, (E i).localize f x).pts = ((⨅ i, E i).localize f x).pts := by
  rw [pts_iInf, pts_localize, pts_iInf, Set.preimage_iUnion]
  simp_rw [pts_localize]

end LocalizeDatum

/-- Remark 1, p. 276: with `N̄ = dim X'_S` and `n̄ = dim W'_S`, the localized datum is a
resolution datum on `X'_S` of type `ℜ^{N̄,n̄}_I` with closed restriction `F'_S` (resp. with
open restriction `U'_S`), resp. of type `ℜ^{N̄}_II` without restriction (resp. with
restriction `F'_S`).

Deviation from the paper (statement modified): `N̄ = dim X'_S` and `n̄ = dim W'_S` are
notations (Def. 3 (iv), p. 164) and the type indices are not part of a datum in this
formalization; the statement asserts that the localized tuples are resolution data (`IsDatum`)
and that the localized restrictions are restrictions for them.  That `X'_S` is a non-singular
irreducible algebraic scheme of dimension `N̄` (the ambient condition of a "resolution datum on
`X'_S`") is not part of this statement: it is proved in `exists_lt_isAmbient_localizeScheme_of_dimAt_ne` /
`exists_lt_isAmbient_localizeScheme_of_dimAt_ne_of_isPermissibleII` (`IsAmbient`), under the hypotheses of the propositions.  The
hypotheses `_hX'` and `IrreducibleSpace X'` are not used.

Gap in the paper filled: the paper gives no proof; the transfer of the density conditions
("`W − F` dense in `W`", "`U` dense in `W`") uses generic points of the irreducible components
of `closure(O ∩ C)`, which lie in the range of `j` (`mem_closure_preimage`). -/
@[blueprint "rem:IV.1-1"
  (statement := /-- \textbf{Remark 1.} Let the notation and assumptions be the same as in
    \cref{def:IV.1}. Let $\bar N=\dim X'_S$ and $\bar n=\dim W'_S$. (I) If
    $\mathfrak R'=(\mathfrak R^{N,n}_{\mathrm I},F')$ (resp.\
    $=(\mathfrak R^{N,n}_{\mathrm I},U')$) then $\mathfrak R'_S$ is a resolution datum on
    $X'_S$ of the type $\mathfrak R^{\bar N,\bar n}_{\mathrm I}$ with closed restriction
    $F'_S$ (resp.\ with open restriction $U'_S$). (II) If
    $\mathfrak R'=\mathfrak R^N_{\mathrm{II}}$ (resp.\
    $=(\mathfrak R^N_{\mathrm{II}},F')$) then $\mathfrak R'_S$ is a resolution datum on
    $X'_S$ of the type $\mathfrak R^{\bar N}_{\mathrm{II}}$ without restriction (resp.\ with
    restriction $F'_S$). (p.\ 276.)

    \textbf{Deviation from the paper (statement modified).} The type indices are not part of a
    datum in Lean, and the statement only asserts that the localized tuples and restrictions
    satisfy Definitions 3 and 5; that $X'_S$ is non-singular, irreducible and of dimension
    $\bar N$ is proved separately in the localized stages of Propositions 1--4. -/)
  (proof := /-- (The paper gives no proof.) By \cref{lem:IV.1-localize-basic} the local
    rings of $X'_S$ and of the induced subschemes are those of $X'$ and of the subschemes of
    $X'$ at the corresponding points, so all the conditions of Definitions 3 and 5 which are
    conditions on those local rings (reducedness, codimension one, normal crossings, normal
    flatness, non-singularity and irreducibility) are inherited.

    \textbf{Gap in the paper filled.} The density conditions on the restrictions ($W'-F'$
    dense in $W'$, $U'$ dense in $W'$) are not local-ring conditions; Lean transfers them using
    that the generic points of the irreducible components of the closure of a locally closed
    set through a point of $X'_S$ lie in $X'_S$ (its range is closed under generization). -/)
  (latexEnv := "remark")]
theorem localize_isDatum {X X' : Scheme.{u}} [IsAlgebraicScheme X] [IsAlgebraicScheme X']
    (f : X' ⟶ X) [LocallyOfFiniteType f] [QuasiCompact f] (_hX' : X'.IsNonsingular)
    [IrreducibleSpace X'] (x : X) :
    (∀ ℜ : DatumI.Raw X', ℜ.IsDatum →
      (ℜ.localize f x).IsDatum ∧
      (∀ F : Subscheme X', ℜ.IsClosedRestriction F →
        (ℜ.localize f x).IsClosedRestriction (F.localize f x)) ∧
      (∀ U : Set X', ℜ.IsOpenRestriction U →
        (ℜ.localize f x).IsOpenRestriction (localizeSet f x U))) ∧
    (∀ ℜ : DatumII.Raw X', ℜ.IsDatum →
      (ℜ.localize f x).IsDatum ∧
      (∀ F : Subscheme X', ℜ.IsClosedRestriction F →
        (ℜ.localize f x).IsClosedRestriction (F.localize f x))) := by
  have hjpts : ∀ (D : Subscheme X') (y : localizeScheme f x),
      y ∈ (D.localize f x).pts ↔ (localizeMap f x) y ∈ D.pts := fun D y => by
    rw [pts_localize]
    rfl
  refine ⟨fun ℜ hℜ => ?_, fun ℜ hℜ => ?_⟩
  · obtain ⟨hEred, hEcodim, hEnc, hWred, hWV⟩ := hℜ
    have hdat : (ℜ.localize f x).IsDatum := by
      refine ⟨localize_isReduced f x _ hEred, fun y hy => ?_, fun y => ?_,
        localize_isReduced f x _ hWred, fun j U => localize_mono f x (fun U => hWV j U) U⟩
      · show (ℜ.E.localize f x).codimAt y = 1
        rw [localize_codimAt]
        exact hEcodim _ ((hjpts _ y).mp hy)
      · have := localize_hasOnlyNormalCrossingsWithAt f x ℜ.E ⊥ y (hEnc _)
        rw [localize_bot] at this
        exact this
    refine ⟨hdat, fun F hF => ?_, fun U hU => ?_⟩
    · obtain ⟨hFn, hEF, hdense⟩ := hF
      refine ⟨localize_isNonsingularIrreducibleCodimOne f x F hFn, fun y => ?_, fun y hy => ?_⟩
      · have := localize_hasOnlyNormalCrossingsWithAt f x (ℜ.E.union F) ⊥ y (hEF _)
        rw [localize_bot] at this
        exact (hasOnlyNormalCrossingsWithAt_congr (localize_pts_inf f x ℜ.E F) ⊥ y).mpr this
      · have hjy : (localizeMap f x) y ∈ ℜ.W.pts := (hjpts _ y).mp hy
        have h1 := hdense hjy
        have heq : ℜ.W.pts \ F.pts = F.ptsᶜ ∩ ℜ.W.pts := by
          ext z
          simp only [Set.mem_sdiff, Set.mem_inter_iff, Set.mem_compl_iff]
          tauto
        rw [heq] at h1
        have h2 := mem_closure_preimage f x F.support.isClosed.isOpen_compl
          ℜ.W.support.isClosed h1
        have heq2 : (ℜ.localize f x).W.pts \ (F.localize f x).pts =
            (localizeMap f x).base ⁻¹' (F.ptsᶜ ∩ ℜ.W.pts) := by
          show (ℜ.W.localize f x).pts \ (F.localize f x).pts = _
          rw [pts_localize, pts_localize]
          ext z
          simp only [Set.mem_sdiff, Set.mem_preimage, Set.mem_inter_iff, Set.mem_compl_iff]
          tauto
        rw [heq2]
        exact h2
    · obtain ⟨⟨U₀, hU₀, rfl⟩, hdense, hres⟩ := hU
      refine ⟨⟨(localizeMap f x).base ⁻¹' U₀, hU₀.preimage (localizeMap f x).base.hom.continuous,
        ?_⟩, fun y hy => ?_, fun y hy => ?_⟩
      · show (localizeMap f x).base ⁻¹' (U₀ ∩ ℜ.W.pts) = _ ∩ (ℜ.W.localize f x).pts
        rw [pts_localize, Set.preimage_inter]
      · have hjy := (hjpts _ y).mp hy
        exact mem_closure_preimage f x hU₀ ℜ.W.support.isClosed (hdense hjy)
      · obtain ⟨hs, hnf, hnc⟩ := hres _ hy
        exact ⟨localize_isSimpleAt f x _ y hs,
          fun j => localize_isNormallyFlatAlongAt' f x _ _ (hWV j) y (hnf j),
          localize_hasOnlyNormalCrossingsWithAt f x _ _ y hnc⟩
  · obtain ⟨hb, hE, hnc, hJ⟩ := hℜ
    have hEU : ((ℜ.localize f x).eUnion).pts = (ℜ.eUnion.localize f x).pts :=
      localize_pts_iInf f x ℜ.E
    have hdat : (ℜ.localize f x).IsDatum := by
      refine ⟨hb, fun i => localize_isNonsingularIrreducibleCodimOne f x _ (hE i), fun y => ?_,
        fun y => localize_stalkIdeal_ne_bot f x ℜ.J y (hJ _)⟩
      have := localize_hasOnlyNormalCrossingsWithAt f x ℜ.eUnion ⊥ y (hnc _)
      rw [localize_bot] at this
      exact (hasOnlyNormalCrossingsWithAt_congr hEU ⊥ y).mpr this
    refine ⟨hdat, fun F hF => ?_⟩
    obtain ⟨hFn, hEF⟩ := hF
    refine ⟨localize_isNonsingularIrreducibleCodimOne f x F hFn, fun y => ?_⟩
    have := localize_hasOnlyNormalCrossingsWithAt f x (ℜ.eUnion.union F) ⊥ y (hEF _)
    rw [localize_bot] at this
    refine (hasOnlyNormalCrossingsWithAt_congr ?_ ⊥ y).mpr this
    rw [← localize_pts_inf]
    unfold Subscheme.union
    rw [pts_inf, pts_inf, hEU]

/-! ### Remark 2 (p. 277) -/

namespace MonoidalSuccession

/-- "A succession of monoidal transformations with nowhere dense centers" (Remark 2,
p. 277): every center `B_i ⊆ X_i` is a nowhere dense subset of `X_i`. -/
def HasNowhereDenseCenters : {X Y : Scheme.{u}} → MonoidalSuccession X Y → Prop
  | _, _, nil _ => True
  | _, _, cons B _ rest => _root_.IsNowhereDense B.pts ∧ rest.HasNowhereDenseCenters

end MonoidalSuccession

/-- A monoidal transformation with a nowhere dense center is surjective: its image is closed
(`lem:monoidal-transformation-proper`) and contains the dense complement of the center, over
which it is an isomorphism. -/
theorem MonoidalTransformation.surjective_of_isNowhereDense [Hironaka.Cited.MonoidalTransformationExistsIsProper.{u}] {X : Scheme.{u}} {B : Subscheme X}
    [IsLocallyNoetherian X] (t : MonoidalTransformation X B) (hB : IsNowhereDense B.pts) :
    Function.Surjective t.f.base := by
  have := t.isProper
  have hint : interior B.pts = ∅ := by
    have h := hB
    unfold IsNowhereDense at h
    rwa [show closure B.pts = B.pts from B.support.isClosed.closure_eq] at h
  have hsub : B.ptsᶜ ⊆ Set.range t.f.base := fun y hy => by
    obtain ⟨y', hy'⟩ := t.exists_apply_eq_of_notMem hy
    exact ⟨y', hy'⟩
  have hcl : IsClosed (Set.range t.f.base) := t.f.isClosedMap.isClosed_range
  have hd : closure B.ptsᶜ = Set.univ := by rw [closure_compl, hint, Set.compl_empty]
  intro y
  exact hcl.closure_subset_iff.mpr hsub (hd ▸ Set.mem_univ y)

/-- A succession of monoidal transformations with nowhere dense centers is surjective. -/
theorem MonoidalSuccession.surjective_composite [Hironaka.Cited.MonoidalTransformationExistsIsProper.{u}] {X Y : Scheme.{u}} [IsLocallyNoetherian X]
    (s : MonoidalSuccession X Y) (hs : s.HasNowhereDenseCenters) :
    Function.Surjective s.composite.base := by
  revert ‹IsLocallyNoetherian X›
  induction s with
  | nil X =>
    intro _
    exact Function.surjective_id
  | cons B t rest ih =>
    intro _
    have := t.isProper
    have : IsLocallyNoetherian t.X' := LocallyOfFiniteType.isLocallyNoetherian t.f
    rw [MonoidalSuccession.composite_cons, Scheme.Hom.comp_base, TopCat.coe_comp]
    exact (t.surjective_of_isNowhereDense hs.1).comp (ih hs.2)

/-- Chains of specializations lift along a closed map of schemes: a chain
`q₀ < q₁ < ⋯ < q_n` (each `q_{i+1}` a proper generization of `q_i`) whose last term is the image
of `t` lifts to a chain of the same length whose first term lies over `q₀` (the image of the
closure of a lift of `q_{i+1}` is closed, hence contains `q_i`). -/
private theorem exists_ltSeries_lift {T S : Scheme.{u}} (π : T ⟶ S) (hcl : IsClosedMap π.base)
    (q : LTSeries S) : ∀ t : T, π t = q.last →
      ∃ r : LTSeries T, r.length = q.length ∧ π r.head = q.head := by
  induction q using RelSeries.inductionOn with
  | singleton x =>
    intro t ht
    exact ⟨RelSeries.singleton _ t, rfl, ht⟩
  | cons p x hx ih =>
    intro t ht
    rw [RelSeries.last_cons] at ht
    obtain ⟨r, hlen, hhead⟩ := ih t ht
    have hsp : p.head ⤳ x := Scheme.le_iff_specializes.mp hx.le
    have hmem : x ∈ π.base '' closure {r.head} :=
      hsp.mem_closed (hcl _ isClosed_closure) ⟨r.head, subset_closure rfl, hhead⟩
    obtain ⟨t', ht'cl, ht'⟩ := hmem
    have hlt : t' < r.head := by
      refine lt_iff_le_not_ge.mpr ⟨Scheme.le_iff_specializes.mpr
        (specializes_iff_mem_closure.mpr ht'cl), fun h => ?_⟩
      have h1 : π t' ⤳ π r.head :=
        (Scheme.le_iff_specializes.mp h).map π.base.hom.continuous
      rw [ht', hhead] at h1
      exact (lt_iff_le_not_ge.mp hx).2 (Scheme.le_iff_specializes.mpr h1)
    exact ⟨r.cons t' hlt, by simp [hlen], by simp [ht']⟩

set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false in
/-- The inequality `dim(S) ≤ dim(X'_S)` of Remark 2 (`rem:IV.1-2`), for a succession with
nowhere dense centers of any scheme: `X'_S → Spec(S)` is closed (a base change of a proper
morphism) and surjective, so every chain of generizations of the closed point of `Spec(S)`
lifts to a chain in `X'_S`. -/
theorem le_dim_localizeScheme [Hironaka.Cited.MonoidalTransformationExistsIsProper.{u}] {X Y : Scheme.{u}} [IsLocallyNoetherian X]
    (s : MonoidalSuccession X Y)
    (hs : s.HasNowhereDenseCenters) (x : X) :
    X.dimAt x ≤ (localizeScheme s.composite x).dim := by
  classical
  set T := localizeScheme s.composite x
  let ι := X.fromSpecStalk x
  let π : T ⟶ Spec (X.presheaf.stalk x) := pullback.snd s.composite ι
  have : Surjective s.composite := ⟨s.surjective_composite hs⟩
  have hπsurj : Surjective π :=
    (inferInstance : Surjective (pullback.snd s.composite (X.fromSpecStalk x)))
  have := s.isProper_composite
  have : IsProper π := MorphismProperty.pullback_snd _ _ inferInstance
  have hπcl : IsClosedMap π.base := π.isClosedMap
  have hι : Topology.IsInducing ι.base := ι.isEmbedding.isInducing
  -- `dim X'_S` is not `⊥`
  obtain ⟨t₀, -⟩ := hπsurj.surj (IsLocalRing.closedPoint (X.presheaf.stalk x))
  have hT0 : (0 : WithBot ℕ∞) ≤ T.dim :=
    (ringKrullDim_nonneg_of_nontrivial (R := T.presheaf.stalk t₀)).trans
      (LocSucc.dimAt_le_dim t₀)
  obtain ⟨D, hD⟩ : ∃ D : ℕ∞, T.dim = D := by
    induction h : T.dim using WithBot.recBotCoe with
    | bot => rw [h] at hT0; exact absurd hT0 (by simp)
    | coe D => exact ⟨D, rfl⟩
  rw [LocSucc.dimAt_eq_coheight, hD]
  refine WithBot.coe_le_coe.mpr (Order.coheight_le_iff.mpr fun p hp => ?_)
  -- the chain `p` consists of generizations of `x`, i.e. of points of `Spec(S)`
  have hrange : ∀ i, p i ∈ Set.range ι.base := fun i => by
    rw [Scheme.range_fromSpecStalk]
    exact Scheme.le_iff_specializes.mp (hp.trans (p.monotone (Fin.zero_le i)))
  let q : LTSeries (Spec (X.presheaf.stalk x)) :=
    ⟨p.length, fun i => (hrange i).choose, fun i => by
      have h : p.toFun i.castSucc < p.toFun i.succ := p.step i
      show (hrange i.castSucc).choose < (hrange i.succ).choose
      rw [lt_iff_le_not_ge, Scheme.le_iff_specializes, Scheme.le_iff_specializes] at h ⊢
      rw [← hι.specializes_iff, ← hι.specializes_iff, (hrange _).choose_spec,
        (hrange _).choose_spec]
      exact h⟩
  obtain ⟨t, ht⟩ := hπsurj.surj q.last
  obtain ⟨r, hrlen, -⟩ := exists_ltSeries_lift π hπcl q t ht
  have h1 : (r.length : ℕ∞) ≤ Order.coheight r.head := Order.length_le_coheight_head
  have h2 : ((Order.coheight r.head : ℕ∞) : WithBot ℕ∞) ≤ T.dim := by
    rw [← LocSucc.dimAt_eq_coheight]
    exact LocSucc.dimAt_le_dim _
  rw [hD] at h2
  have h3 := WithBot.coe_le_coe.mp h2
  rw [hrlen] at h1
  exact h1.trans h3

/-- The inequality `dim(X'_S) ≤ dim(S)` of Remark 2 for any succession of monoidal
transformations of an algebraic scheme: `dim_{x'} X' ≤ dim_{f(x')} X` by the dimension
inequality for the chart algebras (`MonoidalSuccession.dimAt_le_composite_of_isAlgebraicScheme`),
and the points of `X'_S` lie over generizations of `x`. -/
theorem dim_localizeScheme_le [Hironaka.Cited.MonoidalTransformationExistsIsProper.{u}] {X Y : Scheme.{u}} [IsAlgebraicScheme X]
    (s : MonoidalSuccession X Y) (x : X) :
    (localizeScheme s.composite x).dim ≤ X.dimAt x := by
  have := flat_localizeMap s.composite x
  have := isPreimmersion_localizeMap s.composite x
  refine LocSucc.dim_le_of_forall (localizeMap s.composite x) fun z => ?_
  refine (s.dimAt_le_composite_of_isAlgebraicScheme _).trans
    (LocSucc.dimAt_le_of_specializes ?_)
  have : localizeMap s.composite x z ∈ Set.range (localizeMap s.composite x).base := ⟨z, rfl⟩
  rw [range_localizeMap] at this
  exact this

/-- Remark 2, p. 277: if `f : X' → X` is obtained by a succession of monoidal transformations
with nowhere dense centers, then `dim(X'_S) = dim(S)`, the Krull dimension of the local ring
`S = O_{X,x}`; therefore, in Remark 1, `N̄ ≤ N`, with equality only when `dim(X) = dim(S)`.

Formalization note (encoding): `dim(S)` is `X.dimAt x`, which is by definition the Krull
dimension of `O_{X,x}` (p. 163).

Deviation from the paper (statement modified): "in the above Remark 1, `N̄ ≤ N`" is stated with
`N = dim X`, whereas the `N` of Remark 1 is the type of `ℜ'` on `X'`, i.e. `dim X'` (the two
agree for a succession with nowhere dense centers: `dim_eq_of_hasNowhereDenseCenters`; the
statement with `N = dim X'` as printed is `dim_localizeScheme_le_dim_of_hasNowhereDenseCenters`,
node `rem:IV.1-2-type`).

Gap in the paper filled: the paper gives no proof; `dim(S) ≤ dim(X'_S)` is
`le_dim_localizeScheme` (lifting chains along the closed surjective `X'_S → Spec(S)`) and
`dim(X'_S) ≤ dim(S)` is `dim_localizeScheme_le` (the dimension inequality for the chart algebras
`A[I/a]`, `Hironaka/Compat/LocalizeDim.lean`). -/
@[blueprint "rem:IV.1-2"
  (statement := /-- \textbf{Remark 2.} Let $X$ be an algebraic scheme. Let $f\colon X'\to X$
    be a morphism of algebraic schemes which is obtained by a succession of monoidal
    transformations with nowhere dense centers. Let $x$ be a point of $X$ and $S$ the local
    ring of $X$ at $x$. Then we have $\dim(X'_S)=\dim(S)$ (the Krull dimension of the local
    ring $S$). Therefore, in \cref{rem:IV.1-1}, $\bar N\le N$. The equality occurs only when
    $\dim(X)=\dim(S)$. (p.\ 277.)

    \textbf{Deviation from the paper (statement modified).} The Lean statement reads
    ``$\bar N\le N$'' with $N=\dim X$ (it states $\dim X'_S=\dim S$, $\dim X'_S\le\dim X$, and
    $\dim X'_S=\dim X\Rightarrow\dim X=\dim S$), whereas the $N$ of \cref{rem:IV.1-1} is
    $\dim X'$; both readings are true. -/)
  (proof := /-- (The paper gives no proof.) $X'_S\to\operatorname{Spec}(S)$ is the base change
    of $f$, hence proper; it is surjective, since a monoidal transformation with a nowhere
    dense center is an isomorphism over the dense complement of its center and has closed
    image. Every chain of generizations of the closed point of $\operatorname{Spec}(S)$
    therefore lifts to a chain in $X'_S$, so $\dim(X'_S)\ge\dim(S)$. Conversely, every local
    ring of $X'$ is (a localization of) a ring of the form $A[I/a]$, birational over the local
    ring $A$ of $X$ below it, so $\dim\mathcal O_{X',x'}\le\dim\mathcal O_{X,f(x')}$ by the
    dimension inequality; since the points of $X'_S$ lie over generizations of $x$, this gives
    $\dim(X'_S)\le\dim(S)$. Since $\dim(S)=\dim_x(X)\le\dim(X)=N$, we get $\bar N\le N$, with
    equality only if $\dim(X)=\dim(S)$.

    \textbf{Gap in the paper filled.} The paper asserts the remark without proof; the
    inequality $\dim(X'_S)\le\dim(S)$ needs the dimension inequality
    $\operatorname{ht}\mathfrak P\le\operatorname{ht}(\mathfrak P\cap A)$ for the chart
    algebras $A[I/a]$ (Matsumura, Th.~15.5), and $\dim(X'_S)\ge\dim(S)$ the surjectivity of a
    monoidal transformation with nowhere dense center. -/)
  (latexEnv := "remark")]
theorem dim_localizeScheme_of_nowhereDenseCenters [Hironaka.Cited.MonoidalTransformationExistsIsProper.{u}] {X Y : Scheme.{u}} [IsAlgebraicScheme X]
    (s : MonoidalSuccession X Y) (hs : s.HasNowhereDenseCenters) (x : X) :
    (localizeScheme s.composite x).dim = X.dimAt x ∧
    (localizeScheme s.composite x).dim ≤ X.dim ∧
    ((localizeScheme s.composite x).dim = X.dim → X.dim = X.dimAt x) := by
  have := IsAlgebraicScheme.isNoetherian X
  have heq := le_antisymm (dim_localizeScheme_le s x) (le_dim_localizeScheme s hs x)
  exact ⟨heq, heq ▸ LocSucc.dimAt_le_dim x, fun h => h.symm.trans heq⟩

/-- A succession of monoidal transformations with nowhere dense centers of an algebraic scheme
does not change the dimension: `dim X' = dim X`.  (`dim X' ≤ dim X` by the dimension inequality
`dim_{y} X' ≤ dim_{f(y)} X`; `dim X ≤ dim X'` since `dim_x X = dim(X'_S) ≤ dim X'`, Remark 2.)

Gap in the paper filled: the paper's "`N`" in "in the above Remark 1, `N̄ ≤ N`" is the type of `ℜ'`
on `X'`, i.e. `dim X'`, and the paper does not say that `dim X' = dim X`; see
`dim_localizeScheme_le_dim_of_hasNowhereDenseCenters`. -/
theorem dim_eq_of_hasNowhereDenseCenters [Hironaka.Cited.MonoidalTransformationExistsIsProper.{u}] {X Y : Scheme.{u}} [IsAlgebraicScheme X]
    (s : MonoidalSuccession X Y) (hs : s.HasNowhereDenseCenters) : Y.dim = X.dim := by
  have := IsAlgebraicScheme.isNoetherian X
  refine le_antisymm (iSup_le fun y => ?_) (iSup_le fun x => ?_)
  · exact (s.dimAt_le_composite_of_isAlgebraicScheme y).trans (LocSucc.dimAt_le_dim _)
  · have := flat_localizeMap s.composite x
    have := isPreimmersion_localizeMap s.composite x
    rw [← (dim_localizeScheme_of_nowhereDenseCenters s hs x).1]
    exact LocSucc.dim_le_of_forall (localizeMap s.composite x) fun z => LocSucc.dimAt_le_dim _

/-- Remark 2, p. 277, with the `N` of Remark 1 as printed: if `f : X' → X` is obtained by a
succession of monoidal transformations with nowhere dense centers, then `dim(X'_S) = dim(S)`;
"therefore, in the above Remark 1, `N̄ ≤ N`", where `N = dim X'` is the type of `ℜ'` on `X'`
(`IsAmbient X' N`), "the equality occurs only when `dim(X) = dim(S)`".

This is `dim_localizeScheme_of_nowhereDenseCenters` (where the `N` of the conclusion is read as
`dim X`) together with `dim X' = dim X` (`dim_eq_of_hasNowhereDenseCenters`), which the paper does
not record. -/
@[blueprint "rem:IV.1-2-type"
  (statement := /-- \textbf{Remark 2} (with the $N$ of \cref{rem:IV.1-1} as printed).
    Let $X$ be an algebraic scheme. Let $f\colon X'\to X$ be a morphism of algebraic schemes
    which is obtained by a succession of monoidal transformations with nowhere dense centers.
    Let $x$ be a point of $X$ and $S$ the local ring of $X$ at $x$. Then we have
    $\dim(X'_S)=\dim(S)$. Therefore, in \cref{rem:IV.1-1}, $\bar N\le N$, where
    $\bar N=\dim X'_S$ and $N=\dim X'$ is the type of $\mathfrak R'$ on $X'$. The equality
    occurs only when $\dim(X)=\dim(S)$. (p.\ 277.) -/)
  (proof := /-- (The paper gives no proof.) \cref{rem:IV.1-2} gives $\dim(X'_S)=\dim(S)$,
    $\dim(X'_S)\le\dim X$ and ``$\dim(X'_S)=\dim X$ only if $\dim X=\dim S$''; and
    $\dim X'=\dim X$.

    \textbf{Gap in the paper filled.} The paper's $N$ is $\dim X'$ and it does not say that
    $\dim X'=\dim X$ for such a succession. This holds: $\dim_{y}X'\le\dim_{f(y)}X$ for
    every $y\in X'$ (the dimension inequality for the chart algebras), so $\dim X'\le\dim X$;
    and $\dim_xX=\dim(X'_S)\le\dim X'$ for every $x\in X$, so $\dim X\le\dim X'$. -/)
  (latexEnv := "remark")]
theorem dim_localizeScheme_le_dim_of_hasNowhereDenseCenters [Hironaka.Cited.MonoidalTransformationExistsIsProper.{u}] {X Y : Scheme.{u}} [IsAlgebraicScheme X]
    (s : MonoidalSuccession X Y) (hs : s.HasNowhereDenseCenters) (x : X) :
    (localizeScheme s.composite x).dim = X.dimAt x ∧
    (localizeScheme s.composite x).dim ≤ Y.dim ∧
    ((localizeScheme s.composite x).dim = Y.dim → Y.dim = X.dimAt x) := by
  obtain ⟨h1, h2, h3⟩ := dim_localizeScheme_of_nowhereDenseCenters s hs x
  have hd := dim_eq_of_hasNowhereDenseCenters s hs
  refine ⟨h1, hd ▸ h2, fun h => ?_⟩
  rw [hd]
  exact h3 (hd ▸ h)

/-! ### Lemma 1 (p. 277) -/

/-- Transfer of "the closure of a point is an irreducible component" along an embedding. -/
private theorem closure_singleton_mem_irreducibleComponents_of_isEmbedding {A B : Type*}
    [TopologicalSpace A] [TopologicalSpace B] {ι : A → B} (hι : Topology.IsEmbedding ι)
    {S : Set B} (hS : IsClosed S) (hrange : ∀ a, ι a ∈ S) (a : A)
    (hmax : ∀ T : Set B, IsIrreducible T → IsClosed T → T ⊆ S → closure {ι a} ⊆ T →
      T ⊆ closure {ι a}) :
    closure {a} ∈ irreducibleComponents A := by
  refine ⟨isIrreducible_singleton.closure, fun T hT hle => ?_⟩
  have h1 : closure (ι '' T) ⊆ closure {ι a} := by
    refine hmax _ (hT.image ι hι.continuous.continuousOn).closure isClosed_closure
      (closure_minimal (Set.image_subset_iff.mpr fun t _ => hrange t) hS) ?_
    exact closure_mono (Set.singleton_subset_iff.mpr ⟨a, hle (subset_closure rfl), rfl⟩)
  intro t ht
  rw [hι.isInducing.closure_eq_preimage_closure_image, Set.image_singleton]
  exact h1 (subset_closure ⟨t, ht, rfl⟩)

/-- If `W ⊆ V`, then the subscheme `W ×_X V` of `V` induced by a reduced `W` is reduced. -/
private theorem totalTransform_ι_isReduced {X : Scheme.{u}} (V W : Subscheme X) (hW : W.IsReduced)
    (hWV : W.IsContainedIn V) : (Subscheme.totalTransform V.ι W).IsReduced := by
  have hle : V ≤ W := fun U => hWV U
  have hW' : W.subschemeι = Scheme.IdealSheafData.inclusion hle ≫ V.subschemeι :=
    (Scheme.IdealSheafData.inclusion_subschemeι hle).symm
  have : IsIso (pullback.snd V.subschemeι W.subschemeι) := by
    rw [hW']
    infer_instance
  have : IsReduced W.toScheme := hW
  let e := Scheme.IdealSheafData.comapIso W V.subschemeι
  have : IsIso (e.hom ≫ pullback.snd V.subschemeι W.subschemeι) := inferInstance
  have : IsOpenImmersion (e.hom ≫ pullback.snd V.subschemeι W.subschemeι) :=
    IsOpenImmersion.of_isIso _
  have key : IsReduced (W.comap V.subschemeι).subscheme :=
    isReduced_of_isOpenImmersion (e.hom ≫ pullback.snd V.subschemeι W.subschemeι)
  exact key

/-- The points of `W ×_X V` are the points of `V` lying on `W`. -/
private theorem pts_totalTransform_ι {X : Scheme.{u}} (V W : Subscheme X) :
    (Subscheme.totalTransform V.ι W).pts = V.ι ⁻¹' W.pts := by
  change ((W.comap V.subschemeι).support : Set V.toScheme) = _
  rw [Scheme.IdealSheafData.support_comap]
  rfl

/-- Normal flatness of `V` along a reduced `W ⊆ V` is an open condition on `W`
(Cor. of Th. 1, II §1, applied on `V`). -/
private theorem exists_isOpen_normallyFlat' {X : Scheme.{u}} [IsAlgebraicScheme X]
    (V W : Subscheme X) (hW : W.IsReduced) (hWV : W.IsContainedIn V) :
    ∃ O : Set X, IsOpen O ∧ ∀ y ∈ W.pts, (Subscheme.IsNormallyFlatAlongAt' V W y ↔ y ∈ O) := by
  have := isAlgebraicScheme_toScheme V
  obtain ⟨U, ⟨U₀, hU₀, rfl⟩, -, hU⟩ := Subscheme.exists_isOpen_dense_isNormallyFlatAlong
    (X := V.toScheme) (Subscheme.totalTransform V.ι W) (totalTransform_ι_isReduced V W hW hWV)
  obtain ⟨O, hO, hOU⟩ := V.ι.isEmbedding.isInducing.isOpen_iff.mp hU₀
  refine ⟨O, hO, fun y hy => ⟨?_, fun hyO => ?_⟩⟩
  · rintro ⟨x', rfl, hx'⟩
    have := (hU x' hx'.1).mpr hx'
    rw [← hOU] at this
    exact this.1
  · have hyV : y ∈ Set.range V.ι := by
      rw [Scheme.IdealSheafData.range_subschemeι]
      exact pts_subset_of_isContainedIn hWV hy
    obtain ⟨x', rfl⟩ := hyV
    have hx'tt : x' ∈ (Subscheme.totalTransform V.ι W).pts := by
      rw [pts_totalTransform_ι]
      exact hy
    refine ⟨x', rfl, (hU x' hx'tt).mp ⟨?_, hx'tt⟩⟩
    rw [← hOU]
    exact hyO

/-- The openness half of Lemma 1 (`lem:IV.1-1`): the resolved points of `W` form an open
subset of `W`.  The argument (simple points, `cor:II.1-thm1`, `lem:normal-crossings-open-paper`)
uses neither the irreducibility of `X` nor the form `(⋃ E_i; V; W)` of the datum; this is the
form in which Lemma 1 is applied in the proofs of Propositions 1–4, to data
`(⋃ E_i; V, W; B'')` built in the course of those proofs. -/
theorem DatumI.Raw.exists_isOpen_resolvedSet [Hironaka.Cited.IsHironakaBaseIsClosedSingularLocus.{u}] {X : Scheme.{u}} [IsAlgebraicScheme X]
    (hX : X.IsNonsingular) (ℜ : DatumI.Raw X) (hℜ : ℜ.IsDatum) :
    ∃ U₀ : Set X, IsOpen U₀ ∧ {y ∈ ℜ.W.pts | ℜ.ResolvedAt y} = U₀ ∩ ℜ.W.pts := by
  obtain ⟨hEred, hEcod, -, hWred, hWV⟩ := hℜ
  -- the simple points of `W`
  have := isAlgebraicScheme_toScheme ℜ.W
  obtain ⟨Os, hOs, hOsW⟩ :=
    ℜ.W.ι.isEmbedding.isInducing.isOpen_iff.mp (isOpen_setOf_isSimpleAt ℜ.W.toScheme)
  have hsimple : ∀ y ∈ ℜ.W.pts, ℜ.W.IsSimpleAt y ↔ y ∈ Os := by
    intro y hy
    have hy' : y ∈ Set.range ℜ.W.ι := by
      rw [Scheme.IdealSheafData.range_subschemeι]
      exact hy
    obtain ⟨y', rfl⟩ := hy'
    obtain ⟨e⟩ := nonempty_stalk_quot_equiv ℜ.W y'
    rw [← Set.mem_preimage, hOsW]
    constructor
    · rintro ⟨-, h⟩
      exact IsRegularLocalRing.of_ringEquiv e
    · intro h
      have : IsRegularLocalRing (ℜ.W.toScheme.presheaf.stalk y') := h
      exact ⟨hy, IsRegularLocalRing.of_ringEquiv e.symm⟩
  -- normal flatness
  choose Onf hOnf hnf using fun j => exists_isOpen_normallyFlat' (ℜ.V j) ℜ.W hWred (hWV j)
  -- normal crossings (`lem:normal-crossings-open-paper`, Lemma 1 as printed)
  have hnc : ∃ Onc : Set X, IsOpen Onc ∧
      ∀ y ∈ ℜ.W.pts, (ℜ.E.HasOnlyNormalCrossingsWithAt ℜ.W y ↔ y ∈ Onc) := by
    choose! Uy hUy hyUy hUyW using fun y (h : ℜ.E.HasOnlyNormalCrossingsWithAt ℜ.W y) =>
      Subscheme.exists_isOpen_hasOnlyNormalCrossingsWithAt_of_isReduced hX _ _ hEred hEcod hWred y h
    refine ⟨⋃ y ∈ {y | ℜ.E.HasOnlyNormalCrossingsWithAt ℜ.W y}, Uy y,
      isOpen_biUnion fun y hy => hUy y hy, fun y hy => ⟨fun h => ?_, fun h => ?_⟩⟩
    · exact Set.mem_biUnion h (hyUy y h)
    · obtain ⟨z, hz, hyz⟩ := Set.mem_iUnion₂.mp h
      exact hUyW z hz y ⟨hyz, hy⟩
  obtain ⟨Onc, hOnc, hncW⟩ := hnc
  refine ⟨Os ∩ (⋂ j, Onf j) ∩ Onc,
    (hOs.inter (isOpen_iInter_of_finite hOnf)).inter hOnc, ?_⟩
  ext y
  simp only [Set.mem_ofPred_eq, Set.mem_inter_iff, Set.mem_iInter, DatumI.Raw.ResolvedAt]
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨hyW, hs, hnfj, hn⟩
    exact ⟨⟨⟨(hsimple y hyW).mp hs, fun j => (hnf j y hyW).mp (hnfj j)⟩,
      (hncW y hyW).mp hn⟩, hyW⟩
  · rintro ⟨⟨⟨hs, hnfj⟩, hn⟩, hyW⟩
    exact ⟨hyW, (hsimple y hyW).mpr hs, fun j => (hnf j y hyW).mpr (hnfj j),
      (hncW y hyW).mpr hn⟩

/-- `lem:IV.1-1` in the form used by the lifting constructions of
`Hironaka/Compat/LocalizeSuccession.lean`. -/
theorem resolvedSetIsOpen_holds [Hironaka.Cited.IsHironakaBaseIsClosedSingularLocus.{u}] : ResolvedSetIsOpen.{u} := fun _ _ hY ℜ hℜ =>
  DatumI.Raw.exists_isOpen_resolvedSet hY ℜ hℜ

/-- The second half of Lemma 1 (`lem:IV.1-1`): "`ℜ^{N,n}_I` is resolved at the generic points of
irreducible components of `W`" ("It is clear that"), so the set of resolved points of `W` meets
every irreducible component of `W`.  The argument uses neither the expression `E = ⋃ E_i` nor the
irreducibility of `X`; this is the form in which it is applied in the proofs of Propositions 1
and 2, to data `(⋃ E_i; V, W; B'')` built in the course of those proofs
(`LocSucc.lift_transformation`). -/
theorem DatumI.Raw.nonempty_inter_resolvedSet_of_mem_irreducibleComponents {X : Scheme.{u}}
    [IsAlgebraicScheme X] (ℜ : DatumI.Raw X) (hℜ : ℜ.IsDatum) :
    ∀ C ∈ ℜ.W.irreducibleComponents, (C.pts ∩ {y ∈ ℜ.W.pts | ℜ.ResolvedAt y}).Nonempty := by
  obtain ⟨-, -, hEnc, hWred, hWV⟩ := hℜ
  rintro C ⟨Z, hZ, rfl⟩
  obtain ⟨⟨hZirr, hZW⟩, hZmax⟩ := hZ
  set ξ := hZirr.genericPoint with hξdef
  have hξZ : closure {ξ} = (Z : Set X) := by
    rw [(hZirr.isGenericPoint_genericPoint_closure).def, Z.isClosed.closure_eq]
  have hξmem : ξ ∈ (Z : Set X) := by
    rw [← hξZ]
    exact subset_closure rfl
  have hξW : ξ ∈ ℜ.W.pts := hZW hξmem
  have hmax : ∀ T : Set X, IsIrreducible T → IsClosed T → T ⊆ ℜ.W.pts →
      closure {ξ} ⊆ T → T ⊆ closure {ξ} := by
    intro T hT hTc hTW hle
    rw [hξZ] at hle ⊢
    exact hZmax (y := ⟨T, hTc⟩) ⟨hT, hTW⟩ hle
  -- `W_ξ` is the maximal ideal
  have hξ' : ξ ∈ Set.range ℜ.W.ι := by
    rw [Scheme.IdealSheafData.range_subschemeι]
    exact hξW
  obtain ⟨ξ', hξ'ξ⟩ := hξ'
  have hWξ : ℜ.W.stalkIdeal ξ = IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (X.presheaf.stalk ξ) := by
    rw [← hξ'ξ]
    refine stalkIdeal_eq_maximalIdeal_of_isReduced ℜ.W hWred ξ' ?_
    refine closure_singleton_mem_irreducibleComponents_of_isEmbedding ℜ.W.ι.isEmbedding
      ℜ.W.support.isClosed (fun a => ?_) ξ' ?_
    · rw [← Scheme.IdealSheafData.range_subschemeι]
      exact ⟨a, rfl⟩
    · rw [hξ'ξ]
      exact hmax
  refine ⟨ξ, ?_, hξW, ?_, fun j => ?_, ?_⟩
  · show ξ ∈ ((Scheme.IdealSheafData.vanishingIdeal Z).support : Set X)
    rw [Scheme.IdealSheafData.coe_support_vanishingIdeal]
    exact hξmem
  · refine ⟨hξW, ?_⟩
    rw [hWξ]
    show IsRegularLocalRing (IsLocalRing.ResidueField (X.presheaf.stalk ξ))
    infer_instance
  · -- normal flatness of `V_j` along `W` at `ξ`
    have hξV : ξ ∈ Set.range (ℜ.V j).ι := by
      rw [Scheme.IdealSheafData.range_subschemeι]
      exact pts_subset_of_isContainedIn (hWV j) hξW
    obtain ⟨x', hx'ξ⟩ := hξV
    set tt := Subscheme.totalTransform (ℜ.V j).ι ℜ.W with htt
    have htt_pts : tt.pts = (ℜ.V j).ι ⁻¹' ℜ.W.pts := pts_totalTransform_ι _ _
    have hx'tt : x' ∈ tt.pts := by
      rw [htt_pts]
      show (ℜ.V j).ι x' ∈ ℜ.W.pts
      rw [hx'ξ]
      exact hξW
    have hx'r : x' ∈ Set.range tt.ι := by
      rw [Scheme.IdealSheafData.range_subschemeι]
      exact hx'tt
    obtain ⟨ξ'', hξ''⟩ := hx'r
    have httξ : tt.stalkIdeal x' =
        IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal ((ℜ.V j).toScheme.presheaf.stalk x') := by
      rw [← hξ'']
      refine stalkIdeal_eq_maximalIdeal_of_isReduced tt
        (totalTransform_ι_isReduced _ _ hWred (hWV j)) ξ'' ?_
      refine closure_singleton_mem_irreducibleComponents_of_isEmbedding
        ((ℜ.V j).ι.isEmbedding.comp tt.ι.isEmbedding) ℜ.W.support.isClosed
        (fun a => ?_) ξ'' ?_
      · have : tt.ι a ∈ tt.pts := by
          show tt.ι a ∈ (tt.support : Set _)
          rw [← Scheme.IdealSheafData.range_subschemeι]
          exact ⟨a, rfl⟩
        rw [htt_pts] at this
        exact this
      · show ∀ T : Set X, IsIrreducible T → IsClosed T → T ⊆ ℜ.W.pts →
          closure {(ℜ.V j).ι (tt.ι ξ'')} ⊆ T → T ⊆ closure {(ℜ.V j).ι (tt.ι ξ'')}
        rw [hξ'', hx'ξ]
        exact hmax
    refine ⟨x', hx'ξ, hx'tt, fun p => ?_⟩
    rw [httξ]
    let := Ideal.Quotient.field
      (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal ((ℜ.V j).toScheme.presheaf.stalk x'))
    exact Module.Free.of_divisionRing _ _
  · -- normal crossings of `E` with `W` at `ξ`
    obtain ⟨z, hz, hcomp, -⟩ := hEnc ξ
    exact ⟨z, hz, hcomp, z, subset_rfl, hWξ.trans hz.1.symm⟩

/-- Lemma 1 (both halves) in the form used by the lifting constructions of Propositions 1 and 2
of `Hironaka/Compat/LocalizeSuccession.lean` (`Lemma1Holds`). -/
theorem lemma_one_holds [Hironaka.Cited.IsHironakaBaseIsClosedSingularLocus.{u}] : Lemma1Holds.{u} := fun _ _ _ hY ℜ hℜ =>
  ⟨DatumI.Raw.exists_isOpen_resolvedSet hY ℜ hℜ,
    DatumI.Raw.nonempty_inter_resolvedSet_of_mem_irreducibleComponents ℜ hℜ⟩

/-- Lemma 1, p. 277: the set `U` of points of `W` at which `ℜ^{N,n}_I` is resolved is an open
subset of `W` which has non-empty intersection with every irreducible component of `W`.

Formalization note (encoding): "`U` is an open subset of `W`" is, as in Definition 5 (I.2),
the existence of an open subset `U₀` of `X` with `U = U₀ ∩ W`; "has non-empty intersection with
every irreducible component of `W`" uses `Subscheme.irreducibleComponents`.

Proof as printed (p. 277): "It is clear that `ℜ^{N,n}_I` is resolved at the generic points of
irreducible components of `W`" (the second conjunct,
`nonempty_inter_resolvedSet_of_mem_irreducibleComponents`); "We have only to prove that `U` is an open
subset of `W`.  First of all, we know that the set of simple points of `W` forms an open subset of `W`"
(`isOpen_setOf_isSimpleAt`, class 𝔅 (iii)); "By Theorem 1 of Ch. II, the set of points of `W` at which
`V₁, …, V_β` are normally flat along `W` is an open subset of `W`" (`cor:II.1-thm1`,
`exists_isOpen_normallyFlat'`); "All left to be proved is that, if `W` has only normal crossings with
`⋃ E_i` at a point `x` of `W`, then there exists an open subset of `W` containing `x` at every point of
which `W` has only normal crossings with `⋃ E_i`" is `lem:normal-crossings-open-paper` (Ch. 0,
`Subscheme.exists_isOpen_hasOnlyNormalCrossingsWithAt_of_isReduced`, for `W` reduced and `E` reduced
everywhere of codimension one, the hypotheses of the datum), whose proof is the printed one (the
paragraph from "Let `Spec(A)` be an affine open subscheme of `X`" on, proved there as printed,
including (2) "`Spec(A) ∩ W` is irreducible …, so that `(z₁, …, z_s)A` is the prime
ideal of `W`"); the union over the points `x` of these neighbourhoods is the open set of the
statement.

No difference in the route.  The hypotheses `E = ⋃ E_i` (`_hE`) and the irreducibility of `X` are
not used, so that this lemma also applies to the data `(⋃ E_i; V, W; B'')` of Propositions 1–4. -/
@[blueprint "lem:IV.1-1"
  (statement := /-- \textbf{Lemma 1.} Let
    $\mathfrak R^{N,n}_{\mathrm I}=(\bigcup_{i=1}^\alpha E_i;V_1,\dots,V_\beta;W)$ be a
    resolution datum of type $\mathfrak R^{N,n}_{\mathrm I}$ on a non-singular irreducible
    algebraic scheme $X$. Let $U$ be the set of points of $W$ at which
    $\mathfrak R^{N,n}_{\mathrm I}$ is resolved. Then $U$ is an open subset of $W$ which has
    non-empty intersection with every irreducible component of $W$. (p.\ 277.) -/)
  (proof := /-- It is clear that $\mathfrak R^{N,n}_{\mathrm I}$ is resolved at the generic
    points of irreducible components of $W$. We have only to prove that $U$ is an open subset
    of $W$. First of all, we know that the set of simple points of $W$ forms an open subset of
    $W$. By Theorem 1 of Ch.\ II (\cref{thm:II.1-1}, in the form \cref{cor:II.1-thm1}), the
    set of points of $W$ at which $V_1,\dots,V_\beta$ are normally flat along $W$ is an open
    subset of $W$. All left to be proved is that, if $W$ has only normal crossings with
    $\bigcup_{i=1}^\alpha E_i$ at a point $x$ of $W$, then there exists an open subset of $W$
    containing $x$ at every point of which $W$ has only normal crossings with
    $\bigcup_{i=1}^\alpha E_i$ (this is \cref{lem:normal-crossings-open-paper}).
    Let $\operatorname{Spec}(A)$ be an affine open subscheme of $X$ which contains the given
    point $x$, where $A$ is an algebra of finite type over a base ring of $X$. Let $P$ be the
    prime ideal in $A$ such that $A_P$ is the local ring of $X$ at $x$. We have a regular
    system of parameters $(z_1,\dots,z_r)$ of $A_P$ such that those $E_i$ passing through $x$
    as well as $W$ have prime ideals in $A_P$ generated by subsystems of $(z_1,\dots,z_r)$.
    We arrange the indices of the $z_j$ in such a way that, for a certain positive integer
    $s\le r$, $(z_1,\dots,z_s)$ generates the prime ideal of $W$ in $A_P$. By replacing $A$ by
    $A_f$ with a suitable $f\in A-P$, so that $\operatorname{Spec}(A_f)$ is an affine open
    subscheme of $X$ containing the given point $x$, we may assume that:
    (1) for every subsystem $(z_{i_1},\dots,z_{i_t})$ of $(z_{s+1},\dots,z_r)$,
    $(z_1,\dots,z_s,z_{i_1},\dots,z_{i_t})A$ is a prime ideal in $A$, and
    $A/(z_1,\dots,z_s,z_{i_1},\dots,z_{i_t})A$ is a regular ring, and
    (2) $\operatorname{Spec}(A)\cap W$ is irreducible (hence, non-singular by (1)), so that
    $(z_1,\dots,z_s)A$ is the prime ideal of $W$ in the affine ring $A$, and
    (3) $\operatorname{Spec}(A)$ has empty intersection with any of the $E_j$ which does not
    pass through $x$.
    Now, if $y$ is any point of $\operatorname{Spec}(A)\cap W$ and if $Q$ denotes the prime
    ideal of $y$ in $A$, then by (1) the subsystem of $(z_1,\dots,z_r)$ consisting of those
    $z_j$ contained in $Q$ can be extended to a regular system of parameters of the local ring
    $A_Q$ of $X$ at $y$, so that, by (2) and (3), $W$ has only normal crossings with
    $\bigcup_{i=1}^\alpha E_i$ at $y$. q.e.d.

    \textbf{Remark.} The normal-crossings paragraph above (from ``Let $\operatorname{Spec}(A)$ be an
    affine open subscheme'' on) is proved as printed in \cref{lem:normal-crossings-open-paper}
    (for $W$ reduced and $E$ reduced everywhere of codimension one, the hypotheses of the datum),
    and applied here; the Lean proof of the openness uses neither the expression
    $E=\bigcup_iE_i$ nor the irreducibility of $X$ (these hypotheses are not used), so that it also
    applies to the data $(\bigcup_iE_i;V,W;B'')$ of Propositions 1--4. -/)
  (latexEnv := "lemma")]
theorem DatumI.Raw.isOpen_resolvedSet [Hironaka.Cited.IsHironakaBaseIsClosedSingularLocus.{u}] {X : Scheme.{u}} [IsAlgebraicScheme X]
    (_hX : X.IsNonsingular) [IrreducibleSpace X] (ℜ : DatumI.Raw X) (hℜ : ℜ.IsDatum)
    (_hE : ℜ.IsUnionOfDivisors) :
    (∃ U₀ : Set X, IsOpen U₀ ∧ {y ∈ ℜ.W.pts | ℜ.ResolvedAt y} = U₀ ∩ ℜ.W.pts) ∧
    ∀ C ∈ ℜ.W.irreducibleComponents,
      (C.pts ∩ {y ∈ ℜ.W.pts | ℜ.ResolvedAt y}).Nonempty := by
  refine ⟨DatumI.Raw.exists_isOpen_resolvedSet _hX ℜ hℜ, ?_⟩
  exact DatumI.Raw.nonempty_inter_resolvedSet_of_mem_irreducibleComponents ℜ hℜ

/-! ### Lemma 2 (p. 278) -/

/-- Lemma 2, p. 278: `S(ℜ^N_II)` and `S_*(ℜ^N_II)` are closed subsets of `X` of codimension at
least one.

Formalization note (encoding): "of codimension at least one" is expressed, exactly as in the
paper's proof, by "the generic point of `X` does not belong to `S(ℜ^N_II)`" (`X` being
irreducible); no separate codimension statement is made.  The paper recalls
`S_*(ℜ) = {x ∈ S(ℜ) | ν(J_x) = ν̄}` with `ν̄ = ν(ℜ)`; this is `DatumII.Raw.sStar`, which is
defined with `≥ ν̄` and coincides with it since `ν̄` is the maximum.

Proof as printed (p. 278): the generic point does not lie on `S(ℜ)` ("Obviously", see
`LocSucc.genericPoint_notMem_S`), and `S_* ⊆ S`; with `P_i` the sheaf of ideals of `E_i` and
`J' = ∏ P_i^{a_i} J` (`DatumII.Raw.jPrime`), "We have `S(ℜ^N_II) = {x ∈ X | ν(J'_x) ≥ b}`"
(`DatumII.Raw.S_eq_setOf_le_nu_jPrime`), "which is closed in `X` by Corollary 1 of Theorem 2 of §3,
Ch. III" (`Subscheme.isClosed_setOf_le_nu_stalkIdeal`, applied to `J'`); and "`S_*(ℜ^N_II) =
S(ℜ^N_II) ∩ {x ∈ X | ν(J_x) ≥ ν̄}` which is closed, by the same reason" (the same corollary,
applied to `J`).

Gaps in the paper filled: the identity
`ν(J'_x) = ∑_{x∈E_i} a_i + ν(J_x)` behind "We have `S = {ν(J'_x) ≥ b}`" uses `ν(P_{i,x}) = 1`
for `x ∈ E_i` (`Subscheme.IsNonsingularIrreducibleCodimOne.nu_stalkIdeal_eq_one`), `P_{i,x}` the
unit ideal for `x ∉ E_i`, and the additivity `ν(IK) = ν(I) + ν(K)` in a regular local ring
(`Ideal.nu_mul_eq`); the "Obviously" is `LocSucc.genericPoint_notMem_S`. -/
@[blueprint "lem:IV.1-2"
  (statement := /-- \textbf{Lemma 2.} Let
    $\mathfrak R^N_{\mathrm{II}}=\big(E_1,\dots,E_\alpha\,\big|\,J,b\,\big|\,
    a_1,\dots,a_\alpha\big)$ be a resolution datum of the type $\mathfrak R^N_{\mathrm{II}}$
    on a non-singular irreducible algebraic scheme $X$. Then $S(\mathfrak R^N_{\mathrm{II}})$
    and $S_*(\mathfrak R^N_{\mathrm{II}})$ are closed subsets of $X$ of codimension at least
    one. (p.\ 278.)

    Formalization note (encoding): ``of codimension at least one'' is expressed by ``the generic
    point of $X$ does not belong to the set''; $S_*$ is defined with $\nu(J_x)\ge\bar\nu$,
    which is equivalent since $\bar\nu$ is the maximum. -/)
  (proof := /-- We recall the definition
    $S(\mathfrak R^N_{\mathrm{II}})=\{x\in X\mid\sum_{x\in E_i}a_i+\nu(J_x)\ge b\}$ and, if
    $\bar\nu=\nu(\mathfrak R^N_{\mathrm{II}})=\max_{x\in S(\mathfrak R^N_{\mathrm{II}})}
    \{\nu(J_x)\}$, $S_*(\mathfrak R^N_{\mathrm{II}})=\{x\in S(\mathfrak R^N_{\mathrm{II}})
    \mid\nu(J_x)=\bar\nu\}$. Obviously, the generic point of $X$ does not belong to
    $S(\mathfrak R^N_{\mathrm{II}})$, and $S_*(\mathfrak R^N_{\mathrm{II}})\subseteq
    S(\mathfrak R^N_{\mathrm{II}})$. We have only to prove that
    $S(\mathfrak R^N_{\mathrm{II}})$ and $S_*(\mathfrak R^N_{\mathrm{II}})$ are closed subsets
    of $X$. Let $P_i$ denote the coherent sheaf of ideals of $E_i$ on $X$ for
    $1\le i\le\alpha$. Let $J'=\prod_{i=1}^\alpha P_i^{a_i}J$, which is a coherent sheaf of
    ideals on $X$. We have $S(\mathfrak R^N_{\mathrm{II}})=\{x\in X\mid\nu(J'_x)\ge b\}$,
    which is closed in $X$ by Corollary 1 of Theorem 2 of \S3, Ch.\ III
    (\cref{cor:III.thm2-1}). We have $S_*(\mathfrak R^N_{\mathrm{II}})=
    S(\mathfrak R^N_{\mathrm{II}})\cap\{x\in X\mid\nu(J_x)\ge\bar\nu\}$ which is closed, by
    the same reason. q.e.d.

    \textbf{Gaps in the paper filled.} The identity
    $S(\mathfrak R^N_{\mathrm{II}})=\{x\mid\nu(J'_x)\ge b\}$ uses, without comment, that
    $\nu(P_{i,x})=1$ for $x\in E_i$ ($P_{i,x}$ is a prime of height one with regular quotient,
    generated by part of a regular system of parameters of $\mathcal O_{X,x}$), that $P_{i,x}$ is
    the unit ideal for $x\notin E_i$, and that $\nu(IK)=\nu(I)+\nu(K)$ for ideals of a regular
    local ring ($\mathrm{gr}_M$ is a domain); Lean proves these, and ``obviously, the generic
    point does not belong to $S$'' ($\nu(J_\eta)=0$, no $E_i$ contains $\eta$, $b>0$). -/)
  (latexEnv := "lemma")]
theorem DatumII.Raw.isClosed_S_and_Sstar [Hironaka.Cited.IsHironakaBaseIsClosedSingularLocus.{u}] [Hironaka.Cited.CurveFiniteIntegralClosure.{u}] [Hironaka.Cited.IsRegularLocalRingLocalizationOfIsRegularLocalRing.{u}] {X : Scheme.{u}} [IsAlgebraicScheme X]
    (hX : X.IsNonsingular) [IrreducibleSpace X] (ℜ : DatumII.Raw X) (hℜ : ℜ.IsDatum) :
    IsClosed ℜ.S ∧ IsClosed ℜ.sStar ∧
    genericPoint X ∉ ℜ.S ∧ genericPoint X ∉ ℜ.sStar := by
  -- the steps of the printed proof are in `Hironaka/Compat/LocalizeSuccessionII.lean`
  -- "Obviously, the generic point of `X` does not belong to `S(ℜ^N_II)`, and `S_* ⊆ S`"
  have hη : genericPoint X ∉ ℜ.S := LocSucc.genericPoint_notMem_S hX ℜ hℜ
  -- "`S(ℜ^N_II) = {x ∈ X | ν(J'_x) ≥ b}`, closed by Corollary 1 of Theorem 2 of §3, Ch. III"
  have hS : IsClosed ℜ.S := ℜ.isClosed_S_of_isDatum hX hℜ
  -- "`S_*(ℜ^N_II) = S(ℜ^N_II) ∩ {x ∈ X | ν(J_x) ≥ ν̄}` which is closed, by the same reason"
  have hSstar : IsClosed ℜ.sStar := ℜ.isClosed_sNu_of_isDatum hX hℜ ℜ.nu
  exact ⟨hS, hSstar, hη, fun h => hη h.1⟩

/-! ### The localized stage (pp. 279, 281, 283) -/

section Stage

open MonoidalSuccession

/-- A proper closed subscheme of an irreducible scheme is nowhere dense. -/
theorem Subscheme.isNowhereDense_pts_of_ne_univ {Y : Scheme.{u}} [IrreducibleSpace Y]
    {B : Subscheme Y} (h : B.pts ≠ Set.univ) : IsNowhereDense B.pts := by
  have hcl : IsClosed B.pts := B.support.isClosed
  rw [hcl.isNowhereDense_iff]
  by_contra hint
  obtain ⟨y, hy⟩ := Set.nonempty_iff_ne_empty.mpr hint
  have hdense : Dense (interior B.pts) := isOpen_interior.dense ⟨y, hy⟩
  refine h (Set.eq_univ_of_univ_subset ?_)
  have := hcl.closure_subset_iff.mpr (interior_subset (s := B.pts))
  rw [hdense.closure_eq] at this
  exact this

/-- The permissible successions of Proposition 1 have nowhere dense centers: each center
`B ⊆ F` lies in the proper closed subset `F` of the irreducible scheme.  (Used to apply Remark 2,
`rem:IV.1-2`, p. 277, which is stated for "nowhere dense centers"; the paper does not say that the
centers of a permissible succession are nowhere dense.) -/
theorem MonoidalSuccession.IsPermissibleIClosed.hasNowhereDenseCenters [Hironaka.Cited.MonoidalTransformationExistsIsProper.{u}] {N n : ℕ}
    {X Y : Scheme.{u}} {s : MonoidalSuccession X Y} {ℜ : DatumI.Raw X} (h : IsStageI N n X ℜ)
    {F : Subscheme X} (hF : ℜ.IsClosedRestriction F) (hs : s.IsPermissibleIClosed ℜ F) :
    s.HasNowhereDenseCenters := by
  induction s with
  | nil X => trivial
  | cons B t rest ih =>
    obtain ⟨h', hF'⟩ := IsStageI.transform_closed h hF hs.1 t
    refine ⟨?_, ih h' hF' hs.2⟩
    have := h.1.2.2.1
    have hFne : F.pts ≠ Set.univ := Subscheme.pts_ne_univ_of_codimOne h.1.2.1 hF.1
    exact Subscheme.isNowhereDense_pts_of_ne_univ fun hB => hFne
      (Set.eq_univ_of_univ_subset (hB ▸ fun z hz => (hs.1.2 hz).2))

/-- The permissible successions of Proposition 2 have nowhere dense centers: a center
`B ⊆ W − U` is a proper closed subscheme, since `U` is dense in the non-empty `W`. -/
theorem MonoidalSuccession.IsPermissibleIOpen.hasNowhereDenseCenters [Hironaka.Cited.MonoidalTransformationExistsIsProper.{u}] {N n : ℕ}
    {X Y : Scheme.{u}} {s : MonoidalSuccession X Y} {ℜ : DatumI.Raw X} (h : IsStageI N n X ℜ)
    {U : Set X} (hU : ℜ.IsOpenRestriction U) (hs : s.IsPermissibleIOpen ℜ U) :
    s.HasNowhereDenseCenters := by
  induction s with
  | nil X => trivial
  | cons B t rest ih =>
    obtain ⟨h', hU'⟩ := IsStageI.transform_open h hU hs.1 t
    refine ⟨?_, ih h' hU' hs.2⟩
    have := h.1.2.2.1
    refine Subscheme.isNowhereDense_pts_of_ne_univ fun hB => ?_
    obtain ⟨y, -⟩ := h.1.2.2.1.isIrreducible_univ.nonempty
    have hWU : ∀ z, z ∉ U := fun z hz => (hs.1.2 (hB ▸ Set.mem_univ z)).2 hz
    have hWu : ℜ.W.pts = Set.univ :=
      Set.eq_univ_of_forall fun z => (hs.1.2 (hB ▸ Set.mem_univ z)).1
    have := hU.2.1 (by rw [hWu]; exact Set.mem_univ y)
    rw [Set.eq_empty_of_forall_notMem hWU, closure_empty] at this
    exact this

/-- The permissible successions of Propositions 3 and 4 have nowhere dense centers: each center
`B ⊆ S_*(ℜ)` lies in `S(ℜ)`, which misses the generic point of the irreducible scheme
(`LocSucc.genericPoint_notMem_S`).  (Used to apply Remark 2, `rem:IV.1-2`, p. 277, which is stated for
"nowhere dense centers"; the paper does not say that the centers of a permissible succession
are nowhere dense.) -/
theorem MonoidalSuccession.IsPermissibleII.hasNowhereDenseCenters [Hironaka.Cited.IsHironakaBaseIsClosedSingularLocus.{u}] [Hironaka.Cited.MonoidalTransformationExistsIsProper.{u}] [Hironaka.Cited.CurveFiniteIntegralClosure.{u}] [Hironaka.Cited.IsRegularLocalRingLocalizationOfIsRegularLocalRing.{u}] {N : ℕ}
    {X Y : Scheme.{u}} {s : MonoidalSuccession X Y} {ℜ : DatumII.Raw X} (hX : IsAmbient X N)
    (hℜ : ℜ.IsDatum) (hs : s.IsPermissibleII ℜ) : s.HasNowhereDenseCenters := by
  induction s with
  | nil X => trivial
  | cons B t rest ih =>
    obtain ⟨hA, hℜ'⟩ := (MonoidalSuccession.cons B t (MonoidalSuccession.nil _)).isAmbient_transformII
      hX ℜ hℜ ⟨hs.1, trivial⟩
    refine ⟨?_, ih hA hℜ' hs.2⟩
    have := hX.2.2.1
    exact Subscheme.isNowhereDense_pts_of_ne_univ fun h =>
      LocSucc.genericPoint_notMem_S hX.2.1 ℜ hℜ ((hs.1.2.1 (h ▸ Set.mem_univ _)).1)

/-- The localized stage of the proofs of Propositions 1 and 2 (pp. 279, 281).  Let
`f : X' → X` be a succession of monoidal transformations with nowhere dense centers of an
ambient scheme `X` of dimension `N`, `ℜ'` a datum of type `ℜ^{N,n}_I` on `X'` (`dim W' = n`,
`n < N`), and `x = f(x')` with `x' ∈ W'` and `dim_x X ≠ N`.  Let `S` be the local ring of `X` at
`x`.  Then, as printed, `N̄ = dim S` and "`dim X'_S = dim S = N̄ < N`" (Remark 2, `rem:IV.1-2`,
p. 277), `X'_S` is a non-singular irreducible algebraic scheme of dimension `N̄`, and
`n̄ = dim W'_S` satisfies `n̄ < N̄` and `n̄ ≤ n`.

Gap in the paper filled: the paper does not check `n̄ < N̄` and `n̄ ≤ n`, which the induction
hypothesis "Theorems `I₁^{N',n'}` with `n' < N' < N` and `n' ≤ n`" requires (`n̄ < N̄`: the
generic point of `X'` lies in `X'_S` and not on `W'`; `n̄ ≤ n`: `dim W'_S ≤ dim W'`). -/
theorem exists_lt_isAmbient_localizeScheme_of_dimAt_ne [Hironaka.Cited.MonoidalTransformationExistsIsProper.{u}] [Hironaka.Cited.ExistsFlatIsLocalHomAdicCompletionOfFlat.{u}] [Hironaka.Cited.ExistsSurjectiveMvPowerSeriesOfIsAdicComplete.{u}] [Hironaka.Cited.IsRegularLocalRingLocalizationIffRankJacobianEqHeight.{u}] [Hironaka.Cited.IsRegularLocalRingLocalizationOfIsRegularLocalRing.{u}] [Hironaka.Cited.IsRegularLocalRingOfFlatOfIsRegularLocalRing.{u}] (N n : ℕ) (hNn : n < N) {X X' : Scheme.{u}} (hX : IsAmbient X N)
    (f : MonoidalSuccession X X') (hf : f.HasNowhereDenseCenters) (ℜ' : DatumI.Raw X')
    (hstage : IsStageI N n X' ℜ') (x : X) (hxN : X.dimAt x ≠ (N : WithBot ℕ∞)) (x' : X')
    (hx' : x' ∈ ℜ'.W.pts) (hfx : f.composite x' = x) :
    ∃ Nb nb : ℕ, nb < Nb ∧ Nb < N ∧ nb ≤ n ∧ X.dimAt x = (Nb : WithBot ℕ∞) ∧
      IsAmbient (localizeScheme f.composite x) Nb ∧
      (ℜ'.localize f.composite x).n = (nb : WithBot ℕ∞) := by
  obtain ⟨hX', hℜ', hWn⟩ := hstage
  have := hX.1
  have := hX'.1
  have := hX'.2.2.1
  have := IsAlgebraicScheme.isNoetherian X
  have := f.isProper_composite
  set j := localizeMap f.composite x
  have := flat_localizeMap f.composite x
  have := isPreimmersion_localizeMap f.composite x
  have hrange := range_localizeMap f.composite x
  have hx'r : x' ∈ Set.range j.base := by
    rw [hrange]
    show f.composite x' ⤳ x
    rw [hfx]
  obtain ⟨z₀, hz₀⟩ := hx'r
  have : Nonempty (localizeScheme f.composite x) := ⟨z₀⟩
  have hZalg : IsAlgebraicScheme (localizeScheme f.composite x) :=
    (isAlgebraicScheme_localizeScheme_and_isEmbedding_localizeMap f.composite x).1
  have hZns := LocSucc.isNonsingular j hX'.2.1
  have hZirr := irreducibleSpace_of_flat_preimmersion j
  -- `N̄ = dim S`, `dim S < N`
  obtain ⟨m, hm, hmN⟩ := LocSucc.exists_nat_of_le (d := X.dimAt x) (N := N)
    (fun h => by
      have h2 : (0 : WithBot ℕ∞) ≤ X.dimAt x := ringKrullDim_nonneg_of_nontrivial
      rw [h] at h2
      exact absurd h2 (by simp))
    ((LocSucc.dimAt_le_dim x).trans hX.2.2.2.le)
  have hmN' : m < N := lt_of_le_of_ne hmN fun h => hxN (by rw [hm, h])
  -- "`dim X'_S = dim S = N̄`" (Remark 2, p. 277)
  have hZm : (localizeScheme f.composite x).dim = (m : WithBot ℕ∞) :=
    (dim_localizeScheme_of_nowhereDenseCenters f hf x).1.trans hm
  -- `W'_S`
  set WS := Subscheme.totalTransform j ℜ'.W
  have hWSne : WS.pts.Nonempty := ⟨z₀, by
    show z₀ ∈ (Subscheme.totalTransform j ℜ'.W).pts
    rw [FlatPreimm.pts_totalTransform]
    show j z₀ ∈ ℜ'.W.pts
    rw [hz₀]
    exact hx'⟩
  have hWlt : ℜ'.W.dim < X'.dim := by
    rw [hX'.2.2.2]
    exact (show ℜ'.W.dim = n from hWn).trans_lt (by exact_mod_cast hNn)
  have hη := LocSucc.genericPoint_notMem_of_dim_lt hWlt
  obtain ⟨zη, hzη⟩ : genericPoint X' ∈ Set.range j.base :=
    FlatPreimm.mem_range_of_specializes j (genericPoint_specializes _) ⟨z₀, rfl⟩
  have hWSu : WS.pts ≠ Set.univ := by
    intro h
    have : zη ∈ WS.pts := h ▸ Set.mem_univ _
    rw [FlatPreimm.pts_totalTransform] at this
    exact hη (hzη ▸ this)
  have h1 : WS.dim + 1 ≤ (localizeScheme f.composite x).dim :=
    LocSucc.dim_add_one_le_of_pts_ne_univ hWSu hWSne
  have hWSn : WS.dim ≤ (n : WithBot ℕ∞) :=
    (LocSucc.dim_totalTransform_le j ℜ'.W).trans_eq hWn
  obtain ⟨nb, hnb, -⟩ := LocSucc.exists_nat_of_le (Subscheme.dim_ne_bot hWSne) hWSn
  rw [hnb, hZm] at h1
  rw [hnb] at hWSn
  have h1' : nb + 1 ≤ m := by exact_mod_cast h1
  have hWSn' : nb ≤ n := by exact_mod_cast hWSn
  exact ⟨m, nb, by omega, hmN', hWSn', hm, ⟨hZalg, hZns, hZirr, hZm⟩, hnb⟩

/-- The improvement step of the proof of Proposition 1 (pp. 278–280): if `f(F' ∩ W')` contains
a point `x` at which `X` has dimension `< N`, a further succession `f'`, permissible for
`f*(ℜ, F)`, removes `x` from `g(F'' ∩ W'')`, `g = f ∘ f'`.

The proof follows the printed one: `N̄ = dim S`, `dim X'_S = dim S = N̄ < N` (Remark 2, via
`exists_lt_isAmbient_localizeScheme_of_dimAt_ne`), Theorem `I₁^{N̄,n̄}` on `X'_S` gives `f̄`, and
`f̄` is lifted to `f'` by `LocSucc.lift_succession_closed` (the induction on `j` with
"(1)–(3)", p. 279; at each step `B''` is the smallest irreducible subscheme with
`B̄_b = (B'')_S`, `dim(B'') < dim(_bW') = n`, `U''` is open dense in `B''` by Lemma 1, and
Theorem `I₂^{N,n''}` gives `h`, p. 280). -/
theorem exists_isPermissibleIClosed_append_notMem_image [Hironaka.Cited.IsHironakaBaseIsClosedSingularLocus.{u}] [Hironaka.Cited.MonoidalTransformationExistsIsProper.{u}] [Hironaka.Cited.ExistsFlatIsLocalHomAdicCompletionOfFlat.{u}] [Hironaka.Cited.ExistsSurjectiveMvPowerSeriesOfIsAdicComplete.{u}] [Hironaka.Cited.IsRegularLocalRingLocalizationIffRankJacobianEqHeight.{u}] [Hironaka.Cited.IsRegularLocalRingLocalizationOfIsRegularLocalRing.{u}] [Hironaka.Cited.IsRegularLocalRingOfFlatOfIsRegularLocalRing.{u}] (N n : ℕ) (hNn : n < N)
    (hI₁ : ∀ N' n' : ℕ, n' < N' → N' < N → n' ≤ n → FundamentalTheorem.I₁.{u} N' n')
    (hI₂ : ∀ n'' : ℕ, n'' < n → FundamentalTheorem.I₂.{u} N n'')
    {X : Scheme.{u}} (hX : IsAmbient X N) {ℜ : DatumI.Raw X} (hstage : IsStageI N n X ℜ)
    {F : Subscheme X} (hF : ℜ.IsClosedRestriction F) {X' : Scheme.{u}}
    (f : MonoidalSuccession X X') (hf : f.IsPermissibleIClosed ℜ F) (x : X)
    (hx : x ∈ f.composite.base '' ((f.strictTransform F).pts ∩ (f.transformI ℜ).W.pts))
    (hxN : X.dimAt x ≠ (N : WithBot ℕ∞)) :
    ∃ (X'' : Scheme.{u}) (f' : MonoidalSuccession X' X''),
      f'.IsPermissibleIClosed (f.transformI ℜ) (f.strictTransform F) ∧
      x ∉ (f.append f').composite.base ''
        (((f.append f').strictTransform F).pts ∩ ((f.append f').transformI ℜ).W.pts) := by
  obtain ⟨x', ⟨hx'F, hx'W⟩, hfx⟩ := hx
  obtain ⟨hstage', hF'⟩ := IsStageI.succession_closed f hstage hF hf
  have hnd : f.HasNowhereDenseCenters := hf.hasNowhereDenseCenters hstage hF
  obtain ⟨Nb, nb, hnN, hNN, hnn, -, hZ, hnbdim⟩ :=
    exists_lt_isAmbient_localizeScheme_of_dimAt_ne N n hNn hX f hnd _ hstage' x hxN x' hx'W hfx
  have hX' := hstage'.1
  have hℜ' := hstage'.2.1
  have := hX.1
  have := hX'.1
  have := hX'.2.2.1
  have := IsAlgebraicScheme.isNoetherian X
  have := f.isProper_composite
  set j := localizeMap f.composite x
  have := flat_localizeMap f.composite x
  have := isPreimmersion_localizeMap f.composite x
  obtain ⟨hdatS, hFS, -⟩ := (localize_isDatum f.composite hX'.2.1 x).1 _ hℜ'
  -- Theorem `I₁^{N̄, n̄}` on `X'_S`
  obtain ⟨Za, sb, hsb, hempty⟩ := hI₁ Nb nb hnN hNN hnn _ hZ ⟨_, hdatS⟩ _
    (hFS _ hF') hnbdim
  -- lifting `f̄` to `X'` ("(1)–(3)", p. 279)
  obtain ⟨X'', f', j', hfl, hpre, hperm, hr, hℜ'', hst⟩ :=
    LocSucc.lift_succession_closed lemma_one_holds N n hI₂ sb j (f.transformI ℜ)
      (f.strictTransform F) hstage' hF' hsb
  refine ⟨X'', f', hperm, ?_⟩
  rintro ⟨y, ⟨hyF, hyW⟩, hgy⟩
  rw [composite_append, Scheme.Hom.comp_apply] at hgy
  have hyr : f'.composite y ∈ Set.range j.base := by
    rw [range_localizeMap]
    show f.composite (f'.composite y) ⤳ x
    rw [hgy]
  rw [← Set.mem_preimage, ← hr] at hyr
  obtain ⟨z, rfl⟩ := hyr
  rw [strictTransform_append] at hyF
  rw [transformI_append] at hyW
  have h1 : z ∈ (Subscheme.totalTransform j'
      (f'.strictTransform (f.strictTransform F))).pts := by
    rw [FlatPreimm.pts_totalTransform]
    exact hyF
  have h2 : z ∈ ((f'.transformI (f.transformI ℜ)).pullback j').W.pts := by
    rw [DatumI.Raw.pullback_W, FlatPreimm.pts_totalTransform]
    exact hyW
  rw [hst] at h1
  rw [hℜ''] at h2
  exact (Set.eq_empty_iff_forall_notMem.mp hempty) z ⟨h2, h1⟩

/-- The improvement step of the proof of Proposition 2 (pp. 280–282): if the image `f(T')` of
the set `T'` of points at which `f*(ℜ)` is not resolved contains a point `x` at which `X` has
dimension `< N`, a further succession `f'`, permissible for `f*(ℜ, U)`, gives
`g(T'') ⊆ f(T')` and `x ∉ g(T'')`, `g = f ∘ f'`.  ("In the following arguments we may replace
`U'` by `W' − T'`", p. 281.) -/
theorem exists_isPermissibleIOpen_append_notMem_image_unresolvedSet [Hironaka.Cited.IsHironakaBaseIsClosedSingularLocus.{u}] [Hironaka.Cited.MonoidalTransformationExistsIsProper.{u}] [Hironaka.Cited.ExistsFlatIsLocalHomAdicCompletionOfFlat.{u}] [Hironaka.Cited.ExistsSurjectiveMvPowerSeriesOfIsAdicComplete.{u}] [Hironaka.Cited.IsRegularLocalRingLocalizationIffRankJacobianEqHeight.{u}] [Hironaka.Cited.IsRegularLocalRingLocalizationOfIsRegularLocalRing.{u}] [Hironaka.Cited.IsRegularLocalRingOfFlatOfIsRegularLocalRing.{u}] (N n : ℕ) (hNn : n < N)
    (hI₂' : ∀ N' n' : ℕ, n' < N' → N' < N → n' ≤ n → FundamentalTheorem.I₂.{u} N' n')
    (hI₂ : ∀ n'' : ℕ, n'' < n → FundamentalTheorem.I₂.{u} N n'')
    {X : Scheme.{u}} (hX : IsAmbient X N) {ℜ : DatumI.Raw X} (hstage : IsStageI N n X ℜ)
    {U : Set X} (hU : ℜ.IsOpenRestriction U) {X' : Scheme.{u}}
    (f : MonoidalSuccession X X') (hf : f.IsPermissibleIOpen ℜ U) (x : X)
    (hx : x ∈ f.composite.base '' (f.transformI ℜ).unresolvedSet)
    (hxN : X.dimAt x ≠ (N : WithBot ℕ∞)) :
    ∃ (X'' : Scheme.{u}) (f' : MonoidalSuccession X' X''),
      f'.IsPermissibleIOpen (f.transformI ℜ) (f.transformOpen U) ∧
      f'.composite.base '' ((f.append f').transformI ℜ).unresolvedSet ⊆
        (f.transformI ℜ).unresolvedSet ∧
      x ∉ (f.append f').composite.base '' ((f.append f').transformI ℜ).unresolvedSet := by
  obtain ⟨x', ⟨hx'W, hx'res⟩, hfx⟩ := hx
  obtain ⟨hstage', hU'⟩ := IsStageI.succession_open f hstage hU hf
  have hnd : f.HasNowhereDenseCenters := hf.hasNowhereDenseCenters hstage hU
  set ℜ' := f.transformI ℜ with hℜ'def
  have hX' := hstage'.1
  have hℜ' := hstage'.2.1
  have := hX.1
  have := hX'.1
  have := hX'.2.2.1
  have := IsAlgebraicScheme.isNoetherian X
  have := f.isProper_composite
  -- the open restriction `W' − T'`
  set Un : Set X' := {y ∈ ℜ'.W.pts | ℜ'.ResolvedAt y} with hUndef
  have hUUn : f.transformOpen U ⊆ Un := by
    intro y hy
    obtain ⟨⟨U₀, -, hUeq⟩, -, hres⟩ := hU'
    refine ⟨?_, hres y hy⟩
    rw [hUeq] at hy
    exact hy.2
  have hUn : ℜ'.IsOpenRestriction Un :=
    ⟨resolvedSetIsOpen_holds X' hX'.1 hX'.2.1 ℜ' hℜ', hU'.2.1.trans (closure_mono hUUn),
      fun y hy => hy.2⟩
  obtain ⟨Nb, nb, hnN, hNN, hnn, -, hZ, hnbdim⟩ :=
    exists_lt_isAmbient_localizeScheme_of_dimAt_ne N n hNn hX f hnd _ hstage' x hxN x' hx'W hfx
  set j := localizeMap f.composite x
  have := flat_localizeMap f.composite x
  have := isPreimmersion_localizeMap f.composite x
  obtain ⟨hdatS, -, hUS⟩ := (localize_isDatum f.composite hX'.2.1 x).1 _ hℜ'
  -- Theorem `I₂^{N̄, n̄}` on `X'_S`
  obtain ⟨Za, sb, hsb, hresS⟩ := hI₂' Nb nb hnN hNN hnn _ hZ ⟨_, hdatS⟩ _
    (hUS _ hUn) hnbdim
  -- lifting `f̄` to `X'`
  obtain ⟨X'', f', j', hfl, hpre, hperm, hr, hℜ''⟩ :=
    LocSucc.lift_succession_open lemma_one_holds N n hI₂ sb j ℜ' Un hstage' hUn hsb
  obtain ⟨hstage'', hUn''⟩ := IsStageI.succession_open f' hstage' hUn hperm
  refine ⟨X'', f', hperm.mono hUUn, ?_, ?_⟩
  · rintro _ ⟨y, ⟨hyW, hyres⟩, rfl⟩
    rw [transformI_append] at hyW hyres
    rw [MonoidalSuccession.transformI_W] at hyW
    have hyW' : f'.composite y ∈ ℜ'.W.pts := f'.pts_strictTransform_subset _ hyW
    refine ⟨hyW', fun hres => hyres ?_⟩
    refine hUn''.2.2 y ?_
    rw [transformOpen_eq]
    exact ⟨hyW', hres⟩
  · rintro ⟨y, ⟨hyW, hyres⟩, hgy⟩
    rw [composite_append, Scheme.Hom.comp_apply] at hgy
    rw [transformI_append] at hyW hyres
    have hyr : f'.composite y ∈ Set.range j.base := by
      rw [range_localizeMap]
      show f.composite (f'.composite y) ⤳ x
      rw [hgy]
    rw [← Set.mem_preimage, ← hr] at hyr
    obtain ⟨z, rfl⟩ := hyr
    have hdat'' := hstage''.2.1
    apply hyres
    rw [← DatumI.Raw.resolvedAt_pullback_iff j' _ hdat''.2.2.2.2, hℜ'']
    refine hresS z ?_
    show z ∈ (sb.transformI (ℜ'.pullback j)).W.pts
    rw [← hℜ'', DatumI.Raw.pullback_W, FlatPreimm.pts_totalTransform]
    exact hyW

