/-- The improvement step of the proof of Proposition 3 (pp. 282–285): if
`f(S_ν(f*ℜ) ∩ F')` contains a point `x` at which `X` has dimension `< N`, a further succession
`f'`, permissible for `f*(ℜ, F)`, removes `x` from `g(S_ν(g*ℜ) ∩ F'')`, `g = f ∘ f'`.  As printed
